00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:54.690
HOLDEN HEALTH CARE COVERAGE
PROVIDER DIRECTORIES.

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:56.340
PLEASE PROCEED WHEN READY, SIR.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:06.240
&GT;&GT; GOOD AFTERNOON, MR.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:06.990
CHAIRMAN.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:10.200
AND I'D LIKE TO THANK YOU AND
THIS COMMITTEE

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.750
FOR YOUR ATTENTION TO CARE OVER

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:15.120
THIS PARTICULAR BILL AND FOR THE
OPPORTUNITY

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.160
TO PRESENT IT TODAY TO YOU.

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:20.760
AB 236 IS MY GHOST NETWORK
PREVENTION BILL,

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:23.700
WHICH WILL ADDRESS RAMPANT
INACCURACIES

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.250
IN HEALTH PLAN PROVIDER
DIRECTORIES.

00:02:26.639 --> 00:02:28.830
I WANT TO BEGIN BY THANKING THE
CHAIR AND COMMITTEE

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:31.350
STAFF FOR WORKING WITH MY
OFFICE.

00:02:31.889 --> 00:02:34.020
THE PROPOSED COMMITTEE
AMENDMENTS HELP GET THIS BILL

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.600
TO A BETTER PLACE BY ADDRESSING
RECENT CONCERNS.

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:38.610
AND I'M HAPPY, MORE THAN HAPPY,

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:40.200
TO ACCEPT THE AMENDMENTS.

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:45.630
IN 2015, CALIFORNIA PASSED
SENATE BILL 137,

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:49.110
WHICH CREATED SOME OF THE
STRONGEST STANDARDS

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:51.180
FOR HEALTH PLANS IN THE NATION.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.400
DESPITE THIS, WE'RE STILL SEEING

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.389
HEALTH PLANS MAINTAIN

00:02:54.389 --> 00:02:56.790
INACCURATE PROVIDER REFERRAL
DIRECTORIES,

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.460
A PRACTICE THAT RESTRICTS
CONSUMERS ACCESS

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:01.680
TO PROMISE HEALTH CARE SERVICES.

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:04.230
THESE INACCURATE LISTS ARE

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:05.910
OFTEN REFERRED TO AS GHOST

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:09.389
NETWORKS BECAUSE THEY DO NOT
ACTUALLY EXIST.

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:12.010
IN AN EFFORT TO ELIMINATE THESE
GHOST NETWORKS

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:14.980
AND ADDRESS RAMPANT DIRECTORY
INACCURACIES,

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:18.310
AB 236 WILL ENSURE ACCURATE
PROVIDER

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:20.260
DIRECTORIES SO PATIENTS CAN
EASILY

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:23.020
FIND CARE AND BETTER DECIDE
WHAT PLANS

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:24.730
MEET THEIR HEALTH CARE NEEDS.

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:28.360
TO STREAMLINE THE PROCESS OF
UPDATING PROVIDER

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:30.639
INFORMATION AND TO MAINTAIN
ACCURACY.

00:03:30.669 --> 00:03:34.660
THE BILL GIVES DEPARTMENT OF
DEPARTMENT OF HEALTH,

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:41.020
DMVS AND CDI THE AUTHORITY TO
REQUIRE HEALTH PLANS

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.510
AND INSURERS TO USE CENTRAL
PROVIDER

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:45.190
DIRECTORY UTILITIES.

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:48.430
AB 236 ALSO INCREASES
ACCOUNTABILITY

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:49.810
BY ANNUALLY INCREASING

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:52.090
ACCURACY BENCHMARKS WITH
EFFECTIVE

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:53.530
ENFORCEMENT METHODS.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:56.170
WITH THESE BENCHMARKS, PROVIDER
DIRECTORIES WILL

00:03:56.170 --> 00:04:01.750
BE REQUIRED TO HAVE A 95%
ACCURACY BY JULY 2028.

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:03.880
I WOULD LIKE TO EMPHASIZE THAT
HEALTH

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:05.440
PLANS ARE ALREADY REQUIRED

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:08.320
TO MAINTAIN ACCURATE DIRECTORIES
UNDER CURRENT LAW,

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:10.780
SO EACH HEALTH PLAN SHOULD
STRIVE TO

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:14.470
CLOSE FOR CLOSE TO 100%
ACCURACY.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.620
THE BILL WAS AMENDED TO ADDRESS
RECENT

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:19.990
CONCERNS AND TO DO THE
FOLLOWING.

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:21.970
DELETES REQUIREMENTS FOR
PROVIDERS

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:23.890
TO BE REMOVED FROM THE DIRECTORY

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:25.450
IF THEY HAVE NOT BEEN
FINANCIALLY

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:27.550
COMPENSATED BY THE PLAN.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:30.279
THE BILL PROHIBITS PLANS AND
INSURERS

00:04:30.279 --> 00:04:31.990
FROM USING PROVIDERS FOR

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:34.960
REPORTING TO DEPARTMENTS DATA
NECESSARY

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.089
FOR NETWORK ACCURACY,

00:04:37.089 --> 00:04:39.670
ADEQUACY, TIMELY ACCESS TO CARE,

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:41.710
AND OTHER LAWS AND REGULATIONS.

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:43.180
AS A RESULT, THIS WILL ENSURE

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:44.440
THE STATE HAS THE INFORMATION

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:46.450
NECESSARY TO UNDERSTAND WHICH
PROVIDERS

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:49.120
ARE SEEING PATIENTS IN SPECIFIC
NETWORKS

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:52.150
AND WHERE GAPS IN NETWORK
ADEQUACY ARE.

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:55.330
ADDITIONAL AMENDMENTS ADDRESS
CONCERNS WITH

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:57.670
THE USE OF UTILITIES TO MEET
BENCHMARKS,

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:00.430
AND CLARIFIES AN ERROR IN A
DIRECTORY

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:01.930
SHOULD ONLY BE CONSIDERED

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:05.020
WHEN IT IMPACTS A PATIENT'S
ACCESS TO CARE.

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:07.540
I WOULD LIKE TO STATE THAT I
REMAIN

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.339
COMMITTED TO WORKING WITH

00:05:09.339 --> 00:05:10.690
ALL STAKEHOLDERS TO ENSURE THIS

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:13.360
BILL IS IN A BETTER PLACE,

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:15.100
BUT I BELIEVE THESE AMENDMENTS
ARE

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:16.630
A STEP IN THE RIGHT DIRECTION.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:21.850
WITH ME TO TESTIFY IN SUPPORT
IS SARAH SORKIN,

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:24.220
A LICENSED MARRIAGE AND FAMILY
THERAPIST,

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:29.500
AND CAITLIN VAN VAN VAN DUSEN.

00:05:30.339 --> 00:05:33.370
DINE, POLICY ADVOCATE AND HEALTH

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:35.740
ACCESS CALIFORNIA RESPECTFULLY

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:37.180
ASK FOR YOUR VOTE WHEN YOU HAVE
A QUORUM.

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:38.290
THANK YOU SIR.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:39.520
THANKS FOR JOINING US.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.260
I WON'T TRY THE NAMES, BUT LET
ME

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:42.970
HAVE YOU IDENTIFY YOURSELVES FOR

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:44.230
THE RECORD BEFORE YOU SPEAK,

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:45.640
AND PLEASE PROCEED WHEN READY.

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:53.500
&GT;&GT; OH, I'M SARA SOROKIN.

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:56.200
I'M A LICENSED MARRIAGE AND
FAMILY THERAPIST.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.180
AND AS A MENTAL HEALTH
THERAPIST,

00:05:58.180 --> 00:06:00.760
I HAVE SEEN FIRSTHAND HOW
INACCURATE

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.589
PROVIDER DIRECTORIES OR GHOST

00:06:02.589 --> 00:06:04.690
NETWORKS HARM PATIENTS.

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:06.670
IN MY SIX YEARS AS A TRIAGE

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:08.710
AND CRISIS THERAPIST AT KAISER,

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:11.350
IT WAS A RARE DAY THAT I DID
NOT SPEAK

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:13.510
TO AT LEAST ONE PATIENT
REPORTING.

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:14.920
THEY HAD CALLED THROUGH LISTS

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:16.450
OF MENTAL HEALTH PROVIDERS

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:18.760
IN AN ATTEMPT TO CONNECT TO
TREATMENT.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:20.589
NONE OF THE PROVIDERS WERE
EITHER

00:06:20.589 --> 00:06:22.510
RESPONSIVE OR AVAILABLE.

00:06:22.510 --> 00:06:25.420
ALL THE WHILE, THE PATIENT'S
MENTAL HEALTH CONDITION

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:29.500
HAD WORSENED WITHOUT THE NEEDED
CARE BEING PROVIDED.

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:31.480
THESE WERE PATIENTS EXPERIENCING

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:33.580
ANXIETY DISORDERS, DEPRESSION,

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:34.960
AND POST-TRAUMATIC STRESS,

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:37.180
AMONG OTHER MENTAL HEALTH
CONCERNS.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:38.980
THEY WERE EXPECTED TO CALL
THROUGH

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:41.200
PROVIDER LISTS OF 2550

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:44.560
OR MORE IN AN ATTEMPT TO GET
CONNECTED TO TREATMENT,

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:46.120
EVEN THOUGH THEIR SYMPTOMS MADE

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:48.700
DOING SO EXTREMELY CHALLENGING.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:52.610
WHEN I WORKED AT UCLA'S STUDENT
COUNSELING CENTER,

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:55.010
WE SPENT VALUABLE TIME THAT
COULD HAVE BEEN

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:57.440
USED TO PROVIDE ASSESSMENT OR
TREATMENT,

00:06:57.440 --> 00:06:59.720
CALLING THROUGH LISTS OF
THERAPISTS IN

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:02.330
THE ANTHEM PROVIDER DIRECTORY
IN ORDER

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:04.790
TO CREATE A MORE ACCURATE LIST
OF AVAILABLE

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:06.800
THERAPISTS TO GIVE TO STUDENTS.

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:08.779
TO INCREASE STUDENTS LIKELIHOOD

00:07:08.779 --> 00:07:11.000
OF GETTING CONNECTED TO NEEDED

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.670
CARE THROUGH THE STUDENT HEALTH
INSURANCE PROGRAM.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:16.820
FREQUENTLY, PATIENTS WHO HAVE
THE MEANS END

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:19.100
UP PAYING OUT OF POCKET FOR
PSYCHOTHERAPY

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:21.710
WHEN THEY CANNOT FIND AN
AVAILABLE PROVIDER

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:23.600
COVERED BY THEIR INSURANCE,

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:25.970
AND THOSE UNABLE TO AFFORD
PRIVATE

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:28.100
PAY ARE LEFT WITHOUT TREATMENT.

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:29.660
DESPITE THE FACT THAT HEALTH

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:31.640
INSURERS MUST PROVIDE OUT OF

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:34.910
NETWORK COVERAGE WHEN THEIR
NETWORKS ARE INADEQUATE.

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:37.340
WHAT WE ARE LEFT WITH IS A TWO

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:38.960
TIER HEALTH CARE SYSTEM

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:42.830
IN WHICH INEQUITIES ARE
EXACERBATED AND REINFORCED.

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:46.310
SOME PATIENTS EXPERIENCE SEVERE
NEGATIVE OUTCOMES

00:07:46.310 --> 00:07:48.980
AS A RESULT OF THESE GHOST
NETWORKS.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:52.040
AS AN EXAMPLE, I HAVE EVALUATED

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:53.870
A PATIENT IN AN EMERGENCY

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:57.080
DEPARTMENT WHO HAD ATTEMPTED
SUICIDE AFTER CALLING

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:00.380
THROUGH A LIST OF 50 PROVIDERS
WITHOUT SUCCESS,

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:04.040
LOSING HOPE AND SPIRALING DEEPER
INTO DEPRESSION.

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:06.890
THIS PATIENT NOW HAS THE TRAUMAS

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:08.390
OF A SUICIDE ATTEMPT,

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:10.460
AND HAVING BEEN HARMED BY OUR
HEALTH CARE

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:13.430
SYSTEM TO ADD TO THEIR TREATMENT
NEEDS,

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:15.290
WE WOULD BE NEGLIGENT IF WE

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:16.610
DIDN'T DO EVERYTHING IN OUR

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:18.380
POWER TO ENSURE PATIENTS GET

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:19.550
THE HEALTH CARE THEY NEED,

00:08:19.550 --> 00:08:22.310
PAY FOR, AND ARE LEGALLY
ENTITLED TO.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:25.040
AB 236 WILL HOLD HEALTH
INSURANCE

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:26.360
COMPANIES ACCOUNTABLE

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:29.270
FOR THE ACCURACY OF THEIR
PROVIDER NETWORK LISTS,

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:31.760
WHICH WILL GO FAR IN IMPROVING
ACCESS

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:33.950
TO ESSENTIAL HEALTH CARE
SERVICES.

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:35.179
THANK YOU.

00:08:35.179 --> 00:08:36.050
THANKS FOR YOUR TESTIMONY.

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:36.679
YES, MA'AM.

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:39.340
&GT;&GT; GOOD AFTERNOON, MR.

00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:40.090
CHAIR AND SENATORS.

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:42.520
I'M KATIE VAN DINES WITH HEALTH
ACCESS CALIFORNIA,

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:45.760
AND WE ARE PROUD TO SPONSOR AB
236 HEALTH PLANS.

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:47.380
AND INSURERS ARE REQUIRED TO
MAINTAIN

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:48.760
DIRECTORIES OF THEIR CONTRACTED

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:50.620
PROVIDERS IN ORDER TO FACILITATE

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:51.880
CARE FOR THEIR ENROLLEES.

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:55.300
AND CONSUMERS DESERVE ACCURATE
PROVIDER DIRECTORIES.

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:56.830
BUT AS YOU JUST HEARD,

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:58.179
THESE DIRECTORIES ARE FAILING

00:08:58.179 --> 00:08:59.860
CONSUMERS IN INACCURACIES.

00:08:59.860 --> 00:09:01.929
THEY ARE CREATING BARRIERS TO
CONSUMERS

00:09:01.929 --> 00:09:03.670
ACCESSING THE CARE THAT THEY
NEED.

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:05.320
AS YOU HEARD FROM MR.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:07.420
HOLDEN, CALIFORNIA HAS THE
STRONGEST LAW

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:09.340
IN THE NATION ON PROVIDER
DIRECTORIES.

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:11.140
YET RECENT STUDIES HAVE FOUND
THAT ONE OF

00:09:11.140 --> 00:09:13.540
THESE DIRECTORIES WAS 80%
INACCURATE,

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:15.520
AND MOST HAD INACCURATE
INFORMATION FOR

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:17.800
A QUARTER OR A THIRD OF THEIR
PROVIDERS.

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:20.170
THESE INACCURACIES ARE THE WORST

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:22.059
FOR BEHAVIORAL HEALTH PROVIDERS

00:09:22.059 --> 00:09:25.390
FOR SERVICES THAT ARE ALREADY
SO HARD TO REACH.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:29.480
EB 236 TAKES IMPORTANT STEPS
TO IMPROVE

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:31.370
PROVIDER DIRECTORY ACCURACY.

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:33.320
FIRST, IT GIVES THE DEPARTMENT
OF MANAGED

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:35.270
HEALTH CARE AND CDI THE
AUTHORITY TO

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:37.880
REQUIRE PLANS IN PROVIDERS TO
USE ESSENTIAL

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:39.890
UTILITY OR ESSENTIAL UTILITIES.

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:41.330
IN WITH CENTRAL UTILITIES,

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:42.620
WE CAN ADDRESS THE CONCERNS
WE'VE

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:44.270
BEEN HEARING FROM PROVIDERS

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:45.860
AROUND HOW TIME CONSUMING

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:49.070
IT IS FOR PROVIDERS TO UPDATE
INFORMATION WITH THEIR

00:09:49.070 --> 00:09:51.350
HEALTH PLANS FOR THE PROVIDER
DIRECTORIES,

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:53.030
BECAUSE THEY'RE HEARING SO MANY
FROM

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:54.020
SO MANY DIFFERENT HEALTH PLANS
THAT

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:57.050
THEY'RE CONTRACTED WITH VIA
PHONE CALL,

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:59.780
VIA PHONE CALLS, MAIL, EMAIL.

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:02.750
SECOND, THIS BILL SETS CLEAR AND
ENFORCEABLE

00:10:02.750 --> 00:10:04.040
STANDARDS FOR ACCURACY,

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.710
ANNUALLY INCREASING BENCHMARKS
STARTING AT 60%

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:08.809
AND INCREASING OVER THE NEXT
FIVE YEARS.

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:15.410
YOU MAY HEAR THAT DMHC AND CDI
HAVE EXISTING

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:17.270
AUTHORITY TO REQUIRE THESE
STEPS.

