MAYBE MY COLLEAGUES WILL COME
DOWN FOR THIS.

00:48:41.000 --> 00:48:43.370
&GT;&GT; OR HOPEFULLY SOMEBODY'S
LISTENING SOMEWHERE.

00:48:43.790 --> 00:48:44.420
HOPE SO.

00:48:44.420 --> 00:48:46.370
APPRECIATE YOUR OPTIMISM ON THIS
TOO AS WELL.

00:48:46.400 --> 00:48:47.330
APPRECIATE THAT.

00:48:47.810 --> 00:48:48.590
THANK YOU, MR.

00:48:48.590 --> 00:48:51.260
CHAIR AND MEMBERS, AND GOOD
AFTERNOON.

00:48:51.440 --> 00:48:53.060
I'D LIKE TO THANK THE CHAIR
FOR HIS

00:48:53.060 --> 00:48:54.469
THOUGHTFUL ENGAGEMENT ON THIS

00:48:54.469 --> 00:48:56.540
IMPORTANT BILL AND FOR THE
COMMITTEE

00:48:56.540 --> 00:48:58.640
STAFF'S SIGNIFICANT EFFORT.

00:48:58.670 --> 00:49:01.160
I WILL BE ACCEPTING THE
COMMITTEE AMENDMENTS TODAY.

00:49:01.489 --> 00:49:03.170
ALSO, WHILE SHE'S NOT HERE,

00:49:03.170 --> 00:49:05.150
I WANT TO THANK SENATOR HURTADO.

00:49:05.450 --> 00:49:07.190
I'M PROUD TO ADD HER AS A
PRINCIPAL

00:49:07.190 --> 00:49:08.450
CO-AUTHOR TO THE BILL.

00:49:08.870 --> 00:49:12.170
WHAT IS BEFORE YOU TODAY IS A
PRODUCT OF MANY HOURS

00:49:12.170 --> 00:49:14.870
OF DISCUSSION WITH COMMITTEES
AND STAKEHOLDERS.

00:49:15.440 --> 00:49:18.860
AB 3001 29 IS A BILL TO PROTECT
OUR COMMUNITIES,

00:49:18.860 --> 00:49:21.380
OUR PATIENTS AND ALL HEALTH CARE
CONSUMERS

00:49:21.380 --> 00:49:24.410
FROM POTENTIALLY NEGATIVE
IMPACTS OF PRIVATE

00:49:24.410 --> 00:49:26.390
EQUITY TRANSACTIONS IN HEALTH
CARE.

00:49:27.140 --> 00:49:28.880
THE GOAL OF THIS BILL IS TO
PROTECT

00:49:28.880 --> 00:49:31.370
THE PUBLIC BY ENSURING
COMPATIBLE ACCESS.

00:49:31.370 --> 00:49:32.420
HEALTH MARKETS.

00:49:32.660 --> 00:49:33.830
HEALTH CARE MARKETS.

00:49:34.600 --> 00:49:36.370
PRIVATE EQUITY INVESTMENT IN

00:49:36.370 --> 00:49:37.300
HEALTH CARE HAS INCREASED

00:49:37.300 --> 00:49:39.580
SIGNIFICANTLY OVER THE PAST TWO
DECADES.

00:49:39.910 --> 00:49:41.680
PRIVATE EQUITY INVESTMENT IN
HEALTH

00:49:41.680 --> 00:49:45.160
CARE IN 2021 TOTALED $83
BILLION,

00:49:45.370 --> 00:49:48.310
AND $20 BILLION OF THAT WAS IN
CALIFORNIA.

00:49:48.820 --> 00:49:50.920
COMPARED THAT TO 12,000,000,001

00:49:50.920 --> 00:49:53.710
BILLION, RESPECTIVELY, IN 2005.

00:49:54.530 --> 00:49:56.930
THERE IS SIGNIFICANT EVIDENCE
THAT PRIVATE EQUITY

00:49:56.930 --> 00:50:00.680
INVESTMENT ACROSS ALL OUTCOME
MEASURES HAS MOST

00:50:00.680 --> 00:50:03.290
OFTEN INCREASED COST TO PATIENTS
OR PAYERS,

00:50:03.290 --> 00:50:06.080
AND HAD MIXED TO HARMFUL IMPACTS
ON QUALITY.

00:50:06.920 --> 00:50:09.020
PRIVATE EQUITIES TIMELINES ARE
SHORT,

00:50:09.020 --> 00:50:11.210
OFTEN 3 TO 7 YEARS.

00:50:11.510 --> 00:50:13.730
THE TRANSACTIONS OFTEN USE 60

00:50:13.730 --> 00:50:16.430
TO 80% DEBT TO FINANCE THESE,

00:50:16.430 --> 00:50:18.650
WHICH THEN SHIFTS THE BURDEN
SHIFTS

00:50:18.650 --> 00:50:20.570
AS A BURDEN TO THE ENTITY.

00:50:21.489 --> 00:50:23.350
FOLLOWED BY THE INVESTORS
PROCESS

00:50:23.350 --> 00:50:24.340
OF RESTRUCTURING IN

00:50:24.340 --> 00:50:27.100
ORDER TO MAKE IT MORE ATTRACTIVE
FOR FUTURE BUYERS.

00:50:28.080 --> 00:50:29.640
THAT RESTRUCTURING CAN INCLUDE

00:50:29.640 --> 00:50:30.780
THINGS LIKE NEGATIVELY

00:50:30.780 --> 00:50:33.030
IMPACT PATIENTS AND HEALTH CARE
WORKERS,

00:50:33.030 --> 00:50:34.739
INCLUDING REDUCING STAFF,

00:50:34.980 --> 00:50:37.500
REPLACING STAFF WITH LOWER COST
STAFF,

00:50:37.680 --> 00:50:40.230
SELLING ASSETS AND LIMITING
SERVICES

00:50:40.230 --> 00:50:41.969
PROVIDED SUCH AS MATERNITY,

00:50:41.969 --> 00:50:45.060
LABOR AND DELIVERY, AND
REPRODUCTIVE HEALTH CARE.

00:50:45.960 --> 00:50:47.219
IN MAY OF THIS YEAR.

00:50:47.219 --> 00:50:49.320
STEWARD HEALTH CARE, THE
STRUGGLING HEALTH

00:50:49.320 --> 00:50:51.810
CARE PROVIDER PROVIDER THAT
RELIED ON

00:50:51.810 --> 00:50:54.989
PRIVATE EQUITY TO ACQUIRE ITS
HOSPITALS IN TEXAS,

00:50:54.989 --> 00:50:56.969
FLORIDA AND MASSACHUSETTS.

00:50:56.969 --> 00:50:59.340
I BELIEVE THERE ARE 22 HOSPITALS
IN ALL,

00:50:59.640 --> 00:51:01.260
MOST OF THEM IN SMALL HOSPITALS

00:51:01.260 --> 00:51:03.270
AND RURAL COMMUNITIES FILED

00:51:03.270 --> 00:51:05.130
FOR CHAPTER 11 BANKRUPTCY.

00:51:05.280 --> 00:51:09.510
THEY WERE IN TREMENDOUS DEBT,
ABOUT $1.2 BILLION.

00:51:09.719 --> 00:51:12.390
STEWARD HEALTH CARE WAS FOUNDED
IN 2010 WHEN

00:51:12.390 --> 00:51:16.260
THE PRIVATE EQUITY FIRM CERBERUS
CAPITAL MANAGEMENT

00:51:16.260 --> 00:51:18.750
BOUGHT OUT THE FAILING CARITAS
CHRISTI

00:51:18.780 --> 00:51:21.060
HEALTH CARE SYSTEM IN
MASSACHUSETTS.

00:51:22.700 --> 00:51:23.630
CERBERUS.

00:51:23.630 --> 00:51:24.410
EXCUSE ME.

00:51:24.410 --> 00:51:26.060
OWNED THE HEALTH CARE SYSTEM
FROM

00:51:26.060 --> 00:51:29.420
ABOUT 2010 TO TO ABOUT 2020.

00:51:29.450 --> 00:51:32.360
IT'S TEN YEAR IN ITS TEN YEAR
OWNERSHIP.

00:51:32.450 --> 00:51:34.880
THEY MADE ABOUT $800 MILLION OFF

00:51:34.880 --> 00:51:36.320
ITS INVESTMENT IN STEWART

00:51:36.320 --> 00:51:38.780
WHILE THE HOSPITAL SYSTEM FELL
FURTHER INTO DEBT.

00:51:39.550 --> 00:51:42.520
THOSE HOSPITALS ARE NOW AT RISK
FOR CLOSURE AND EVEN

00:51:42.520 --> 00:51:45.969
MORE THAN THEY WERE BEFORE THE
ACQUISITION.

00:51:46.000 --> 00:51:48.550
THIS IS JUST ONE TROUBLING
EXAMPLE.

00:51:49.270 --> 00:51:51.489
IS MAKING SOMETHING MORE
EFFICIENT BAD?

00:51:51.520 --> 00:51:55.090
NO, BUT WHEN PRIVATE EQUITY
EQUITY PURCHASES

00:51:55.090 --> 00:51:57.820
SEVERAL PRACTICES OR HOSPITALS
IN A REGION,

00:51:57.880 --> 00:51:59.710
ESPECIALLY IN MORE RURAL AREAS,

00:51:59.710 --> 00:52:01.270
IT CAN CREATE A MONOPOLY.

00:52:01.900 --> 00:52:03.730
THAT USES LEVERAGE TO NEGOTIATE

00:52:03.730 --> 00:52:05.380
HIGHER FEES WITH HEALTH PLANS,

00:52:05.380 --> 00:52:08.110
IN TURN INCREASES HEALTH CARE
PREMIUMS TO EMPLOYERS

00:52:08.110 --> 00:52:11.200
AND EMPLOYEES AND TO THE COST
OF HEALTH CARE.

00:52:12.110 --> 00:52:13.700
IT'S IMPORTANT TO UNDERSTAND
THAT THIS BILL

00:52:13.700 --> 00:52:15.860
DOES NOT PREVENT THESE
TRANSACTIONS.

00:52:16.900 --> 00:52:19.239
BUT IT ALLOWS THE ATTORNEY
GENERAL TO REVIEW

00:52:19.239 --> 00:52:22.300
THEM FOR WHAT HAS BECOME WELL
DOCUMENTED.

00:52:22.450 --> 00:52:25.390
DISADVANTAGES OF PRIVATE EQUITY
IN HEALTH CARE.

00:52:26.040 --> 00:52:29.790
YOU KNOW ME, I HOPE I'M A HEALTH
CARE

00:52:29.790 --> 00:52:32.250
PROVIDER WHO HAS FOUGHT FOR
INCREASED

00:52:32.250 --> 00:52:34.050
ACCESS TO QUALITY AND AFFORDABLE
HEALTH

00:52:34.050 --> 00:52:35.610
CARE FOR ALL CALIFORNIANS,

00:52:35.610 --> 00:52:37.650
AND I'VE DUG INTO THESE ISSUES
DEEPLY,

00:52:37.650 --> 00:52:40.170
WHICH WHICH WAS MUCH THOUGHT AND
COMMITMENT.

00:52:40.170 --> 00:52:41.880
I'VE TAKEN ON TOUGH ISSUES,

00:52:41.880 --> 00:52:42.870
AND I'M WILLING TO FIGHT FOR

00:52:42.870 --> 00:52:45.510
WHAT I BELIEVE IS IN THE
PATIENT'S BEST INTEREST.

00:52:45.540 --> 00:52:48.090
I'M DATA DRIVEN, AND THE DATA
SHOWS

00:52:48.090 --> 00:52:49.410
THAT OVERSIGHT IS NEEDED.

00:52:49.650 --> 00:52:50.489
WHY?

00:52:50.760 --> 00:52:52.469
BECAUSE THERE CURRENTLY IS NONE.

00:52:52.920 --> 00:52:55.050
THIS BILL ESTABLISHES THAT
OVERSIGHT,

00:52:55.050 --> 00:52:57.660
AND I'VE WORKED CLOSELY WITH
ATTORNEY GENERAL BONTA,

00:52:57.960 --> 00:53:00.510
THE CHAIR, AND MANY
STAKEHOLDERS,

00:53:00.510 --> 00:53:03.900
INCLUDING THOSE OPPOSED, TO MAKE
THIS A GOOD BILL.

00:53:04.380 --> 00:53:07.590
MANY HANDS IN THE POT CAN BE
FRUSTRATING AT TIMES,

00:53:07.590 --> 00:53:08.790
BUT IN THE PAST TEN YEARS,

00:53:08.790 --> 00:53:11.100
I'VE SEEN IT RESULT IN GOOD
LEGISLATION THAT

00:53:11.100 --> 00:53:13.260
OTHERWISE MAY NOT HAVE THOUGHT
ABOUT.

00:53:13.380 --> 00:53:15.300
WE MAY NOT HAVE THOUGHT ABOUT
IT AT ALL.

00:53:15.630 --> 00:53:18.660
UM, YOU HAVE, YOU HAVE BEFORE
YOU WHAT?

00:53:18.660 --> 00:53:21.480
I HOPE YOU WILL CONSIDER A
THOUGHTFUL BILL.

00:53:21.600 --> 00:53:23.969
WE'RE WORKING THROUGH A COMPLEX
ISSUE AND REMAIN

00:53:23.969 --> 00:53:25.980
COMMITTED TO CONTINUE WORKING
THROUGH IT.

00:53:26.010 --> 00:53:27.989
TODAY I HAVE WITH ME TO TESTIFY

00:53:27.989 --> 00:53:29.580
DEPUTY DEPUTY ATTORNEY GENERAL

00:53:29.580 --> 00:53:32.160
TIFFANY BROKAW FROM THE ATTORNEY
GENERAL'S OFFICE,

00:53:32.160 --> 00:53:37.290
JOINED BY EMILIO VARANINI, WHO
WILL BE AVAILABLE

00:53:37.290 --> 00:53:38.969
TO ANSWER TECHNICAL QUESTIONS.

00:53:38.969 --> 00:53:41.340
AND KATIE VAN DINE'S, POLICY AND
LEGISLATIVE

00:53:41.340 --> 00:53:43.560
ADVOCATE FOR HEALTH CARE, HEALTH
ACCESS.

00:53:43.560 --> 00:53:45.810
CALIFORNIA IS OUR SECOND
WITNESS.

00:53:46.170 --> 00:53:47.070
THANK YOU.

00:53:47.070 --> 00:53:48.120
ASSEMBLY MEMBER.

00:53:48.390 --> 00:53:49.739
UH, PLEASE PROCEED.

00:53:49.739 --> 00:53:51.690
IDENTIFY YOURSELVES FIRST FOR
THE RECORD.

00:53:52.820 --> 00:53:54.200
IT WANTS TO GO FIRST.

00:53:55.120 --> 00:53:55.870
WELCOME.

00:53:56.440 --> 00:53:57.250
THANK YOU.

00:53:57.400 --> 00:53:57.550
UM.

00:53:57.550 --> 00:53:59.920
GOOD AFTERNOON, CHAIR AND
MEMBERS TIFFANY BROKAW,

00:53:59.950 --> 00:54:02.770
DEPUTY ATTORNEY GENERAL AND
LEGISLATIVE ADVOCATE

00:54:02.770 --> 00:54:04.600
AT THE CALIFORNIA DEPARTMENT
OF JUSTICE.

00:54:04.630 --> 00:54:06.100
I'M HERE TODAY ON BEHALF OF

00:54:06.100 --> 00:54:07.810
ATTORNEY GENERAL ROB BONTA,

00:54:07.810 --> 00:54:10.930
WHO IS THE PROUD SPONSOR OF
AB 3129.

00:54:10.930 --> 00:54:13.450
AND I'D FIRST JUST LIKE TO THANK
YOU,

00:54:13.450 --> 00:54:14.980
THE CHAIR AND YOUR STAFF FOR
WORKING

00:54:14.980 --> 00:54:16.420
WITH US ON THESE AMENDMENTS.

00:54:16.420 --> 00:54:18.160
WE REALLY APPRECIATE THE
CONVERSATIONS THAT

00:54:18.160 --> 00:54:20.290
WE'VE HAD TO GET US TO WHERE
WE ARE NOW.

00:54:20.950 --> 00:54:22.960
UM, AS DOCTOR WOOD HAS, YOU
KNOW,

00:54:22.960 --> 00:54:26.050
STATED IN HIS OPENING REMARKS,

00:54:26.050 --> 00:54:28.660
AB 3129 AUTHORIZES THE ATTORNEY

00:54:28.660 --> 00:54:30.610
GENERAL TO REVIEW HEALTH CARE

00:54:30.610 --> 00:54:32.380
TRANSACTIONS INVOLVING PRIVATE

00:54:32.380 --> 00:54:34.090
EQUITY AND HEDGE FUND GROUPS.

00:54:34.090 --> 00:54:36.850
AND IT ALSO REINFORCES THE
EXISTING BAR

00:54:36.850 --> 00:54:39.010
ON THE CORPORATE PRACTICE OF
MEDICINE,

00:54:39.010 --> 00:54:41.200
AS IT APPLIES TO THE
INTERFERENCE

00:54:41.200 --> 00:54:42.340
OF PRIVATE EQUITY GROUPS

00:54:42.340 --> 00:54:45.130
OR HEDGE FUNDS IN THE MEDICAL
CARE OF PATIENTS.

00:54:45.160 --> 00:54:47.800
THE BILL FOCUSES ON PRIVATE
EQUITY BECAUSE

00:54:47.800 --> 00:54:49.719
THE PRIVATE EQUITY BUSINESS
MODEL,

00:54:49.719 --> 00:54:52.690
WHICH IS DESIGNED DESIGNED TO
BUY AN ASSET,

00:54:52.690 --> 00:54:56.440
MAXIMIZE PROFIT PROFITS AND THEN
SELL THAT ASSET,

00:54:56.440 --> 00:54:58.450
HAS CONCERNING EFFECTS WHEN
APPLIED

00:54:58.450 --> 00:54:59.770
TO OUR HEALTH CARE SYSTEM.

00:54:59.770 --> 00:55:02.020
AND THESE TRANSACTIONS HAVE BEEN
HAPPENING

00:55:02.020 --> 00:55:03.880
HAVE DOUBLED IN THE PAST DECADE.

00:55:04.540 --> 00:55:06.670
SO IN THE HEALTH CARE CONTEXT,

00:55:06.670 --> 00:55:08.950
WHAT THIS LOOKS LIKE IS THAT
A PRIVATE

00:55:08.950 --> 00:55:10.330
EQUITY GROUP WILL COME IN

00:55:10.330 --> 00:55:12.820
AND THEY WILL MAKE CUTS TO
STAFF,

00:55:12.820 --> 00:55:16.270
THEY WILL CUT SERVICES, ALL TO
MAXIMIZE PROFITS.

00:55:16.270 --> 00:55:18.550
AND THEN WHEN THAT FACILITY

00:55:18.550 --> 00:55:20.230
OR PROVIDER GROUP IS SOLD,

00:55:20.230 --> 00:55:23.140
THEY ARE OFTENTIMES SUSCEPTIBLE
TO BANKRUPTCY,

00:55:23.140 --> 00:55:25.989
FURTHER CONSOLIDATION OR
SHUTTING DOWN,

00:55:25.989 --> 00:55:28.719
WHICH JEOPARDIZES THE
COMMUNITY'S ACCESS TO CARE.

00:55:29.380 --> 00:55:32.050
AB 3129 WOULD SET UP OVERSIGHT

00:55:32.050 --> 00:55:33.790
OVER THESE TRANSACTIONS,

00:55:33.790 --> 00:55:35.350
WHERE THE ATTORNEY GENERAL WOULD

00:55:35.350 --> 00:55:37.090
HAVE AUTHORITY TO APPROVE,

00:55:37.090 --> 00:55:39.070
DENY OR APPROVE WITH CONDITIONS

00:55:39.070 --> 00:55:40.960
THESE TRANSACTIONS BASED

00:55:40.960 --> 00:55:43.600
ON WHETHER THEY WOULD BE IN THE
PUBLIC INTEREST.

00:55:43.600 --> 00:55:45.550
THE CONDITIONS THAT THE AG WOULD

00:55:45.550 --> 00:55:47.050
PLACE ON A TRANSACTION

00:55:47.050 --> 00:55:50.350
ARE DESIGNED TO KEEP SERVICES
OPEN AND AFFORDABLE.

00:55:50.350 --> 00:55:52.660
SO, FOR EXAMPLE, A CONDITION
THAT

00:55:52.660 --> 00:55:54.219
THE AG USES IN HIS CURRENT

00:55:54.219 --> 00:55:56.440
ROLE REVIEWING NONPROFIT
HOSPITAL

00:55:56.440 --> 00:55:58.150
TRANSACTIONS AND THAT

00:55:58.150 --> 00:56:00.070
WOULD BE USED IN THIS CONTEXT OF

00:56:00.070 --> 00:56:01.660
PRIVATE EQUITY TRANSACTIONS,

00:56:01.660 --> 00:56:04.510
WOULD BE THAT SERVICES WOULD
NEED TO BE MAINTAINED.

00:56:04.510 --> 00:56:07.239
SO YES, THIS TRANSACTION CAN
HAPPEN,

00:56:07.239 --> 00:56:09.969
BUT THE HOSPITAL WOULD NEED TO
CONTINUE SERVING

00:56:09.969 --> 00:56:12.040
MEDI-CAL PATIENTS AND WOULD NEED
TO KEEP

00:56:12.040 --> 00:56:14.170
THEIR LABOR AND DELIVERY UNIT
OPEN.

00:56:14.820 --> 00:56:16.469
A CONDITION THAT ALSO COULD
COME IN

00:56:16.469 --> 00:56:18.960
THE FORM OF PRICE INCREASE CAPS.

00:56:18.960 --> 00:56:21.060
SO YES, THE TRANSACTION CAN
HAPPEN,

00:56:21.060 --> 00:56:24.180
BUT PRICES FOR SERVICES CAN'T
SKYROCKET

00:56:24.180 --> 00:56:25.830
AND BECOME UNAFFORDABLE.

00:56:25.860 --> 00:56:29.040
THIS REVIEW PROCESS IS NOT AN
AUTOMATIC DENIAL.

00:56:29.040 --> 00:56:31.890
THE OVERSIGHT IS TO HELP ENSURE
THAT CALIFORNIANS

00:56:31.890 --> 00:56:33.840
HAVE ACCESS TO AFFORDABLE HEALTH
CARE,

00:56:33.840 --> 00:56:35.670
AND THAT SERVICES REMAIN
AVAILABLE

00:56:35.670 --> 00:56:36.570
TO THOSE WHO NEED IT.

00:56:36.570 --> 00:56:38.130
AND FOR THESE REASONS, WE
RESPECTFULLY

00:56:38.130 --> 00:56:39.150
ASK FOR YOUR VOTE.

00:56:40.700 --> 00:56:41.330
THANK YOU.

00:56:41.330 --> 00:56:42.350
NEXT, PLEASE.

00:56:43.280 --> 00:56:44.989
GOOD AFTERNOON AGAIN, MR.

00:56:44.989 --> 00:56:45.920
CHAIR AND SENATORS.

00:56:45.920 --> 00:56:47.960
I'M KATIE VAN DINES WITH HEALTH
ACCESS CALIFORNIA,

00:56:47.960 --> 00:56:49.130
THE STATEWIDE HEALTH CARE
CONSUMER

00:56:49.130 --> 00:56:50.090
ADVOCACY COALITION,

00:56:50.090 --> 00:56:51.469
AND WE ARE PROUD TO SUPPORT AB

00:56:51.469 --> 00:56:53.660
3129 BY ASSEMBLY MEMBER WOOD.

00:56:53.690 --> 00:56:56.060
FOR MORE THAN 30 YEARS,
ATTORNEYS GENERAL OF BOTH

00:56:56.060 --> 00:56:57.980
PARTIES HAVE HAD THE AUTHORITY
TO APPROVE,

00:56:57.980 --> 00:57:00.800
DENY OR APPROVE WITH CONDITIONS
MERGERS RELATED TO

00:57:00.800 --> 00:57:03.860
NONPROFIT HOSPITALS AND IN THESE
LAST 30 YEARS,

00:57:03.860 --> 00:57:05.780
BETWEEN 80 AND 90% OF THESE
PROPOSED

00:57:05.780 --> 00:57:06.980
MERGERS HAVE BEEN APPROVED,

00:57:06.980 --> 00:57:09.830
MOSTLY WITH CONDITIONS TO
PROTECT CONSUMERS.

00:57:09.830 --> 00:57:11.719
IN WHAT CONDITIONS HAVE AG'S
ASKED

00:57:11.719 --> 00:57:14.390
FOR TO KEEP EMERGENCY ROOMS
OPEN,

00:57:14.390 --> 00:57:16.400
TO KEEP LABOR AND DELIVERY OPEN,

00:57:16.400 --> 00:57:19.130
TO KEEP CARDIAC CARE AND MORE
SERVICES OPEN.

00:57:19.130 --> 00:57:21.620
TO NOT HIKE UP PRICES ON
CONSUMERS.

00:57:21.620 --> 00:57:24.170
TO NOT DROP MEDI-CAL MANAGED
CARE CONTRACTS,

00:57:24.290 --> 00:57:25.820
TO NOT CLOSE HOSPITALS.

00:57:25.820 --> 00:57:27.410
EXACTLY THE SORT OF CONDITIONS

00:57:27.410 --> 00:57:28.760
NEEDED TO PROTECT ACCESS

00:57:28.760 --> 00:57:31.190
TO AFFORDABLE CARE IN THE
AFFECTED COMMUNITY.

00:57:31.460 --> 00:57:33.410
THIS PROCESS IS NOT NEW.

00:57:33.410 --> 00:57:35.060
WHAT IS NEW IS THAT PRIVATE
EQUITY

00:57:35.060 --> 00:57:36.200
IS TAKING OVER HOSPITALS,

00:57:36.200 --> 00:57:38.450
SKILLED NURSING FACILITIES AND
DOCTORS GROUPS,

00:57:38.450 --> 00:57:39.830
AND RESEARCH IS SHOWING THAT
THIS

00:57:39.830 --> 00:57:41.240
CAN LEAD TO PRICE INCREASES,

00:57:41.240 --> 00:57:43.910
DANGEROUS IMPACTS ON QUALITY
AND RISKS FOR

00:57:43.910 --> 00:57:46.520
ACCESS TO CARE AND LOSS OF
SERVICES.

00:57:47.060 --> 00:57:49.880
AB 3129 WOULD SUBJECT PRIVATE
EQUITY TRANSACTIONS

00:57:49.880 --> 00:57:52.190
IN HEALTH CARE TO THE SAME SORT
OF SCRUTINY THAT,

00:57:52.400 --> 00:57:54.560
AND OVERSIGHT THAT NONPROFIT
HOSPITALS

00:57:54.560 --> 00:57:56.600
HAVE BEEN SUBJECT TO FOR
DECADES,

00:57:57.500 --> 00:57:59.990
WHILE THE OFFICE OF HEALTH CARE
AFFORDABILITY,

00:57:59.990 --> 00:58:02.270
OR OHCA, WILL BE REVIEWING
ACQUISITIONS,

00:58:02.270 --> 00:58:04.580
THEY DO NOT HAVE THE AUTHORITY
TO DENY OR CONDITION

00:58:04.580 --> 00:58:07.100
THESE ACQUISITIONS TO PROTECT
CONSUMERS.

00:58:07.190 --> 00:58:10.640
AND WHILE AN AG COULD ENGAGE IN
ANTITRUST LITIGATION

00:58:10.640 --> 00:58:13.790
AFTER AN OCA REVIEW, THIS
LITIGATION TAKES TIME.

00:58:13.790 --> 00:58:15.320
THE LANDMARK SUTTER SETTLEMENT

00:58:15.320 --> 00:58:16.790
TOOK MORE THAN 14 YEARS,

00:58:16.790 --> 00:58:19.160
FAR LONGER THAN THE 60 DAYS
THE AG

00:58:19.190 --> 00:58:21.050
WOULD HAVE AFTER AN OCA REVIEW.

00:58:22.000 --> 00:58:24.070
WE NEED THE AG TO HAVE THE
AUTHORITY TO

00:58:24.070 --> 00:58:25.870
ACT BEFORE AN ACQUISITION
HAPPENS,

00:58:25.870 --> 00:58:28.450
TO PREVENT HARMFUL IMPACTS ON
COMMUNITIES

00:58:28.450 --> 00:58:30.610
AND PROTECT AFFORDABLE ACCESS
TO CARE.

00:58:30.910 --> 00:58:32.560
WHEN THERE IS A MERGER OR
ACQUISITION

00:58:32.560 --> 00:58:33.160
IN HEALTH CARE,

00:58:33.160 --> 00:58:34.930
WE HEAR A LOT OF PROMISES ABOUT

00:58:34.930 --> 00:58:36.310
THE WONDERFUL THINGS THAT WILL
HAPPEN

00:58:36.310 --> 00:58:38.110
FOR THE COMMUNITY INNOVATION,

00:58:38.110 --> 00:58:39.190
EFFICIENCY AND MORE.

00:58:39.190 --> 00:58:40.630
AND WE WANT THOSE THINGS TO
HAPPEN FOR

00:58:40.630 --> 00:58:42.280
THE COMMUNITY AND FOR HEALTH
CARE.

00:58:42.280 --> 00:58:43.690
BUT WE WANT THE ATTORNEY GENERAL

00:58:43.690 --> 00:58:44.650
TO HAVE THE AUTHORITY

00:58:44.650 --> 00:58:46.270
TO HOLD PRIVATE EQUITY
ACCOUNTABLE TO

00:58:46.270 --> 00:58:48.610
THESE PROMISES AND PREVENT THE
NEGATIVE IMPACTS

00:58:48.610 --> 00:58:50.620
THAT WE'RE WORRIED ABOUT FOR
COMMUNITIES.

00:58:50.650 --> 00:58:53.560
I RESPECTFULLY ASK FOR YOUR VOTE
ON AB 3129.

00:58:53.560 --> 00:58:54.310
THANK YOU.

00:58:55.090 --> 00:58:56.230
THANK YOU.

