01:01:22.440 --> 01:01:24.300
AND AS A NON-LAWYER, I AM
PLEASED

01:01:24.300 --> 01:01:25.320
TO BE JOINED BY LOIS

01:01:25.320 --> 01:01:29.130
RICHARDSON OF COUNSEL AND VICE
PRESIDENT AT CCIA.

01:01:29.340 --> 01:01:31.410
SHOULD THERE BE TECHNICAL
QUESTIONS,

01:01:31.410 --> 01:01:33.660
WHILE WE APPRECIATE THE EFFORTS
OF THE CHAIR,

01:01:34.200 --> 01:01:38.430
REMAINS OPPOSED TO 3129 PATIENTS
NEED ACCESS

01:01:38.430 --> 01:01:40.050
TO EFFECTIVE AND RELIABLE HEALTH
CARE,

01:01:40.050 --> 01:01:42.570
AND THESE SERVICES DO DEPEND
ON CONSTANT

01:01:42.570 --> 01:01:44.310
INNOVATION AND INVESTMENT.

01:01:44.310 --> 01:01:46.440
THE STATE SHOULD CONTINUE TO
ENCOURAGE

01:01:46.440 --> 01:01:47.670
INVESTMENT IN CALIFORNIA'S

01:01:47.670 --> 01:01:49.770
FRAGILE HEALTH CARE DELIVERY
SYSTEM

01:01:49.770 --> 01:01:51.450
RATHER THAN DESTABILIZE IT.

01:01:51.450 --> 01:01:53.610
IN RECENT YEARS, CALIFORNIA
HOSPITALS

01:01:53.610 --> 01:01:54.660
HAVE PARTNERED WITH PRIVATE

01:01:54.660 --> 01:01:58.890
ENTITIES TO BRING NEW AND
EXPANDED SERVICES ONLINE.

01:01:58.890 --> 01:02:02.010
AS A RESULT, FOR EXAMPLE,
INPATIENT REHABILITATION

01:02:02.010 --> 01:02:03.150
HOSPITALS HAVE BEEN BUILT

01:02:03.150 --> 01:02:05.220
IN COMMUNITIES INCLUDING
SACRAMENTO,

01:02:05.220 --> 01:02:07.680
IRVINE, ESCONDIDO, AND CENTURY
CITY.

01:02:07.710 --> 01:02:09.750
THIS BILL WOULD CREATE BARRIERS

01:02:09.750 --> 01:02:11.550
TO SUCCESSFUL NEW INVESTMENTS

01:02:11.550 --> 01:02:14.310
SUCH AS THESE WHEN EXACTLY THE
OPPOSITE IS NEEDED.

01:02:14.940 --> 01:02:16.320
UNFORTUNATELY, THE DEPARTMENT OF

01:02:16.320 --> 01:02:17.970
JUSTICE'S EXISTING AUTHORITY

01:02:17.970 --> 01:02:20.040
OVER NONPROFIT HOSPITAL
TRANSACTIONS

01:02:20.040 --> 01:02:21.750
HAS SERVED AS A BARRIER

01:02:21.750 --> 01:02:24.240
FOR INVESTMENT THAT HAS
SIGNIFICANTLY DELAYED

01:02:24.240 --> 01:02:25.980
OR CURTAILED CRITICAL
ACQUISITIONS,

01:02:25.980 --> 01:02:27.690
PUTTING SERVICES IN JEOPARDY.

01:02:27.810 --> 01:02:31.170
ACCESS TO ALL FINANCIAL TOOLS
IS CRITICAL,

01:02:31.170 --> 01:02:32.940
PARTICULARLY IN VULNERABLE
COMMUNITIES,

01:02:32.940 --> 01:02:34.140
WHERE INVESTMENTS ARE NEEDED

01:02:34.140 --> 01:02:35.700
TO SUPPORT UNDER-RESOURCED

01:02:35.700 --> 01:02:37.590
PROVIDERS SO THAT THEY CAN
BETTER

01:02:37.590 --> 01:02:38.940
SERVE THEIR PATIENTS.

01:02:39.420 --> 01:02:41.850
AS AN EXAMPLE OF THE CONCERNS
THAT REMAIN,

01:02:41.850 --> 01:02:43.140
THE PROCESS TO ALLOW

01:02:43.140 --> 01:02:44.790
DISTRESSED ENTITIES TO REQUEST

01:02:44.790 --> 01:02:45.750
A WAIVER FROM THE FULL

01:02:45.750 --> 01:02:48.210
REVIEW IS FLAWED AND USE
CRITERIA

01:02:48.210 --> 01:02:49.440
THAT GO BEYOND OBJECTIVE

01:02:49.440 --> 01:02:51.150
MEASURES USED BY LENDERS TO

01:02:51.150 --> 01:02:53.160
ADDRESS FINANCIAL DISTRESS.

01:02:53.190 --> 01:02:55.230
TO BE ELIGIBLE FOR A WAIVER,

01:02:55.230 --> 01:02:56.850
AN ENTITY MUST PROVE THAT IT'S

01:02:56.850 --> 01:02:58.500
BEEN UNABLE TO PAY ITS BILLS

01:02:58.500 --> 01:03:00.510
FOR THREE YEARS OR MORE,

01:03:00.510 --> 01:03:03.480
AND THAT IT IS AT SUBSTANTIAL
RISK OF LIQUIDATION

01:03:03.480 --> 01:03:05.220
UNDER CHAPTER SEVEN BANKRUPTCY,

01:03:05.220 --> 01:03:08.160
AND THAT IT IS FACING CHAPTER
11 BANKRUPTCY,

01:03:08.160 --> 01:03:09.780
AMONG OTHER CRITERIA.

01:03:10.140 --> 01:03:12.540
THROUGH COVID, WE'VE SEEN JUST
HOW QUICKLY

01:03:12.540 --> 01:03:14.160
HOSPITAL FINANCES CAN CHANGE,

01:03:14.160 --> 01:03:16.560
AND WE QUESTION WHETHER THIS
MULTILAYER WAIVER

01:03:16.560 --> 01:03:19.320
TEST WOULD APPLY ONLY WHEN IT'S
TOO LATE

01:03:19.320 --> 01:03:22.410
TO HELP SAVE THE FINANCIALLY
STRUGGLING ENTITY

01:03:22.410 --> 01:03:24.450
AND PRESERVE ACCESS FOR
PATIENTS.

01:03:24.780 --> 01:03:25.980
ADDITIONALLY, THE STANDARDS

01:03:25.980 --> 01:03:27.810
FOR REVIEW REMAIN UNCLEAR,

01:03:27.810 --> 01:03:29.460
AND THE JUNE 19TH AMENDMENTS DO

01:03:29.460 --> 01:03:31.170
NOT RESOLVE QUESTIONS RELATED

01:03:31.170 --> 01:03:33.840
TO THE APPLICATION OF THE PUBLIC
INTEREST STANDARD.

01:03:33.960 --> 01:03:38.340
WITHOUT CLEAR STANDARDS, WE
WORRY THAT

01:03:38.340 --> 01:03:39.840
ENTITIES WILL STRUGGLE TO
DETERMINE

01:03:39.840 --> 01:03:42.330
WHETHER OR NOT DOJ APPROVAL IS
LIKELY

01:03:42.330 --> 01:03:44.100
TO BE REQUIRED OR GRANTED.

01:03:44.100 --> 01:03:45.720
PARTNERING HEALTH CARE ENTITIES
THAT

01:03:45.720 --> 01:03:47.460
MAY BELIEVE THAT THEY ARE
EXPANDING

01:03:47.460 --> 01:03:50.310
AND PRESERVING PATIENT ACCESS
MAY CONTINUE

01:03:50.310 --> 01:03:52.140
TO FAIL TO RECEIVE APPROVAL.

01:03:52.140 --> 01:03:55.020
AS THE BILL CONTINUES TO ALLOW
THE ATTORNEY

01:03:55.020 --> 01:03:56.520
GENERAL TO CONSIDER, QUOTE,

01:03:56.520 --> 01:03:58.980
ANY OTHER FACTORS THAT THE
ATTORNEY GENERAL

01:03:58.980 --> 01:04:00.810
DETERMINES TO BE OF PUBLIC
BENEFIT.

01:04:01.410 --> 01:04:04.800
WHILE 3129 PUTS AT RISK
INNOVATION

01:04:04.800 --> 01:04:07.170
AND ADDITIONAL INVESTMENT IN
PATIENT CARE.

01:04:07.200 --> 01:04:08.820
FOR THESE REASONS, WE
RESPECTFULLY

01:04:08.820 --> 01:04:09.930
REQUEST YOUR NO VOTE.

01:04:10.570 --> 01:04:11.380
THANK YOU.

01:04:11.380 --> 01:04:12.190
NEXT, PLEASE.

01:04:12.190 --> 01:04:12.460
MR.

01:04:12.460 --> 01:04:14.680
CHAIR, MEMBERS OF THE COMMITTEE,
MARK OPREA.

01:04:14.710 --> 01:04:16.810
I'M HERE ON BEHALF OF THE
AMERICAN

01:04:16.810 --> 01:04:18.340
INVESTMENT COUNCIL.

01:04:18.340 --> 01:04:21.070
WE WANT TO THANK THE CHAIR AND
THE COMMITTEE

01:04:21.070 --> 01:04:23.050
FOR YOUR WORK ON THIS MEASURE,

01:04:23.050 --> 01:04:24.700
AND WE WANT TO THANK THE AUTHOR,

01:04:24.700 --> 01:04:26.080
AS WELL AS THE SPONSORS,

01:04:26.080 --> 01:04:28.300
FOR MEETING WITH US TO REVIEW.

01:04:28.300 --> 01:04:32.050
&GT;&GT; OUR OBJECTIONS TO THE MEASURE
EARLIER THIS WEEK.

01:04:32.380 --> 01:04:34.360
I THINK IT IS FAIR TO SAY THAT

01:04:34.360 --> 01:04:35.950
HEALTH CARE IN CALIFORNIA

01:04:35.950 --> 01:04:38.980
IS UNDERFUNDED AND REDUCING
CAPITAL,

01:04:38.980 --> 01:04:41.320
AS WE BELIEVE THIS MEASURE WILL
DO,

01:04:41.320 --> 01:04:43.750
REDUCES ACCESS AND QUALITY

01:04:43.750 --> 01:04:45.280
CONTRARY TO THE OBJECTIVE,

01:04:45.430 --> 01:04:47.440
THE OBJECTIVES OF THE BILL.

01:04:47.560 --> 01:04:52.330
GIVEN THE RECENT PASSAGE OF
SENATE BILL 184 IN 2022

01:04:52.330 --> 01:04:55.660
TO CREATE THE OFFICE OF HEALTH
CARE AFFORDABILITY.

01:04:55.690 --> 01:04:59.800
ASSEMBLY BILL 3192 ESTABLISHES
AN UNNECESSARY

01:04:59.800 --> 01:05:03.160
PARALLEL REGULATORY NOTIFICATION
PROCESS.

01:05:03.460 --> 01:05:05.620
THE AMERICAN INVESTMENT COUNCIL
HAS SUPPORTED

01:05:05.620 --> 01:05:07.660
AND CONTINUES TO SUPPORT THE
STATE

01:05:07.660 --> 01:05:09.610
OF CALIFORNIA'S EFFORTS TO
ENHANCE

01:05:09.610 --> 01:05:12.130
AND OVERSIGHT OVER
ANTICOMPETITIVE

01:05:12.130 --> 01:05:14.860
TRANSACTIONS AND BAD ACTORS IN

01:05:14.860 --> 01:05:17.410
THE HEALTH CARE INDUSTRY THAT
POSE

01:05:17.410 --> 01:05:19.990
A DEMONSTRABLE THREAT TO HEALTH
CARE ACCESS,

01:05:19.990 --> 01:05:22.030
PRICES, AND COMPETITION.

01:05:22.030 --> 01:05:25.030
FOR EXAMPLE, AIC WAS SUPPORTED

01:05:25.030 --> 01:05:26.890
THE DEVELOPMENT OF THE
REGULATIONS

01:05:26.890 --> 01:05:29.320
TO IMPLEMENT SENATE BILL 184,

01:05:29.320 --> 01:05:30.640
WHICH, AMONG OTHER THINGS,

01:05:30.640 --> 01:05:31.990
ESTABLISHED THE OFFICE OF HEALTH

01:05:31.990 --> 01:05:33.970
CARE AFFORDABILITY TO SUPPORT

01:05:33.970 --> 01:05:36.520
HEALTH CARE AFFORDABILITY
THROUGH THE COLLECTION,

01:05:36.520 --> 01:05:38.860
ANALYSIS AND PUBLICLY REPORTING

01:05:38.860 --> 01:05:40.480
OF DATA OF TOTAL HEALTH

01:05:40.480 --> 01:05:45.310
CARE EXPENDITURES AND
TRANSACTIONS UNDER AB 3129,

01:05:45.310 --> 01:05:47.380
PRIVATE EQUITY GROUPS AND HEDGE
FUNDS

01:05:47.380 --> 01:05:49.360
WOULD BE REQUIRED TO SUBMIT
HEALTH

01:05:49.360 --> 01:05:51.010
CARE TRANSACTION NOTIFICATIONS

01:05:51.010 --> 01:05:54.460
TO THE AG RATHER THAN TO OCA.

01:05:54.490 --> 01:05:57.670
THIS IS UNNECESSARY, AS OCA IS
EMPOWERED

01:05:57.670 --> 01:05:59.470
TO REFER TRANSACTIONS

01:05:59.470 --> 01:06:03.430
THAT THEY FIND PROBLEMATIC TO
THE AG FOR REVIEW.

01:06:03.430 --> 01:06:07.030
IN PARTICULAR, SB 184 PROVIDES
A CLEAR STATEMENT OF

01:06:07.030 --> 01:06:09.880
THE LEGISLATURE'S INTENT IN
ESTABLISHING

01:06:09.910 --> 01:06:11.200
OCA AS FOLLOWS.

01:06:11.200 --> 01:06:14.470
IT IS THE INTENT OF THE
LEGISLATURE TO ESTABLISH

01:06:14.470 --> 01:06:17.020
A SINGLE ENTITY WITHIN STATE
GOVERNMENT,

01:06:17.020 --> 01:06:19.960
CHARGED WITH REFERRING
TRANSACTIONS THAT

01:06:19.960 --> 01:06:22.600
MAY REDUCE MARKET COMPETITION OR

01:06:22.600 --> 01:06:24.610
INCREASE COST TO THE ATTORNEY TO

01:06:24.610 --> 01:06:26.980
THE ATTORNEY GENERAL FOR FURTHER
REVIEW.

01:06:27.100 --> 01:06:32.440
HOWEVER, AB 3129 MATERIALLY
UNDERCUTS OCA'S MANDATE

01:06:32.440 --> 01:06:36.010
BY CREATING AN UNNECESSARY
PARALLEL PROCESS

01:06:36.010 --> 01:06:38.740
BY REQUIRING CERTAIN HEALTH CARE
ENTITIES TO

01:06:38.740 --> 01:06:41.950
FILE NOTICE WITH THE AG RATHER
THAN OCA,

01:06:41.950 --> 01:06:46.630
AND AB 3129 EFFECTIVELY PREVENTS
OCA FROM COLLECTING

01:06:46.630 --> 01:06:48.700
AND REPORTING DATA INFORMATION

01:06:48.700 --> 01:06:49.810
BECAUSE IT WILL NO LONGER

01:06:49.810 --> 01:06:52.870
RECEIVE THAT DATA TO THE
LEGISLATURE AND THE PUBLIC

01:06:52.870 --> 01:06:55.990
REGARDING HEALTH CARE
EXPENDITURES AND COST TRENDS.

01:06:55.990 --> 01:06:58.990
IF WE LOOK AT THE DEFINITION OF
PRIVATE EQUITY,

01:06:58.990 --> 01:07:02.560
IT IS SO BROAD THAT THE THAT THE
THAT THE MEMBERS

01:07:02.560 --> 01:07:05.320
OF THE LEGISLATURE WHO SIT ON
THE DAIS,

01:07:05.320 --> 01:07:06.940
WHO WOULD POOL THEIR MONEY,

01:07:06.940 --> 01:07:10.210
WOULD BE CONSIDERED A PRIVATE
EQUITY GROUP.

01:07:10.240 --> 01:07:13.360
FURTHERMORE, IT EXEMPTS AN
INDIVIDUAL

01:07:13.360 --> 01:07:15.730
SO A SINGLE INDIVIDUAL COULD BUY

01:07:15.730 --> 01:07:18.520
A HOSPITAL AND WOULD NOT BE
REQUIRED

01:07:18.520 --> 01:07:21.100
TO TO GO THROUGH THE PROCESS.

01:07:21.100 --> 01:07:25.000
THE DEFINITION OF TRANSACTION
SUBJECT TO REVIEW ALSO

01:07:25.000 --> 01:07:29.020
COVERS MINOR EVENTS SUCH AS
CHANGES TO THE BOARD.

01:07:29.020 --> 01:07:31.840
WE THINK THIS ADDS AN
UNNECESSARY

01:07:31.840 --> 01:07:33.610
ADMINISTRATIVE PROCESS,

01:07:33.610 --> 01:07:37.060
AND WE WOULD SUGGEST THAT IT
DOES NOTHING TO SATISFY

01:07:37.060 --> 01:07:39.940
THE INTENT OF THE OF THE OF THE
MEASURE.

01:07:39.940 --> 01:07:42.130
AND FINALLY, TO REITERATE

01:07:42.130 --> 01:07:44.650
AND TO SUPPORT THE TESTIMONY

01:07:44.650 --> 01:07:47.050
