01:55:33.710 --> 01:55:35.870
THIS BILL WILL REQUIRE THAT
COMMERCIAL

01:55:35.870 --> 01:55:37.400
HEALTH PLANS INCLUDE COVERAGE

01:55:37.400 --> 01:55:39.890
FOR MEDICALLY NECESSARY
PASTEURIZED

01:55:39.890 --> 01:55:41.090
DONOR HUMAN MILK,

01:55:41.090 --> 01:55:44.030
WHICH IS COMMONLY REFERRED TO
AS DONOR MILK.

01:55:44.360 --> 01:55:47.180
IF THE DONOR MILK IS SOURCED
FROM A MILK BANK

01:55:47.180 --> 01:55:49.250
WITH AN EXISTING TISSUE BANK
LICENSE,

01:55:49.250 --> 01:55:51.530
THE BILL WAIVES THE REQUIREMENT
FOR HOSPITALS

01:55:51.530 --> 01:55:53.780
TO ACQUIRE THE SAME LICENSE TO

01:55:53.780 --> 01:55:56.390
PROVIDE DONOR MILK TO INFANTS
IN NEONATAL

01:55:56.390 --> 01:55:58.610
INTENSIVE CARE UNITS, OR NICUS.

01:55:58.880 --> 01:56:01.640
THE AMERICAN ACADEMY OF
PEDIATRICS RECOMMENDS THAT

01:56:01.640 --> 01:56:04.040
WHEN A MOTHER'S OWN MILK IS NOT
AVAILABLE,

01:56:04.040 --> 01:56:05.750
THAT DONOR MILK BE PROVIDED TO

01:56:05.750 --> 01:56:08.150
VERY LOW BIRTH WEIGHT INFANTS.

01:56:08.150 --> 01:56:12.110
THESE ARE VERY SMALL INFANTS
THAT WEIGH £3.3

01:56:12.110 --> 01:56:13.370
OR LESS AT BIRTH.

01:56:13.760 --> 01:56:16.520
DONOR MILK IS USED IN NICUS TO
SUPPORT THE HEALTH

01:56:16.520 --> 01:56:19.010
AND SURVIVAL OF VERY LOW BIRTH
WEIGHT INFANTS,

01:56:19.010 --> 01:56:20.660
AND HAS BEEN SHOWN TO REDUCE

01:56:20.660 --> 01:56:22.520
THE INCIDENCE OF A DEVASTATING

01:56:22.520 --> 01:56:24.560
BOWEL DISEASE KNOWN AS
NECROTIZING

01:56:24.560 --> 01:56:26.480
ENTEROCOLITIS OR NEC.

01:56:26.630 --> 01:56:28.460
THE INCIDENCE OF NEC IS AROUND

01:56:28.460 --> 01:56:30.230
60% HIGHER FOR HISPANIC

01:56:30.230 --> 01:56:33.320
AND BLACK INFANTS WHEN COMPARED
TO WHITE INFANTS.

01:56:33.440 --> 01:56:35.120
BLACK AND HISPANIC MOTHERS HAVE

01:56:35.120 --> 01:56:36.770
LOWER RATES OF PROVIDING MILK

01:56:36.770 --> 01:56:38.780
TO THEIR BABIES IN THE NICU DUE

01:56:38.780 --> 01:56:40.070
TO A VARIETY OF FACTORS,

01:56:40.070 --> 01:56:43.670
INCLUDING HAVING TO RETURN TO
WORK, SIBLING CARE,

01:56:43.670 --> 01:56:45.410
LACK OF TRANSPORTATION,

01:56:45.410 --> 01:56:49.010
LESS LACTATION SUPPORT OR
RECEIVING LESS CARE,

01:56:49.010 --> 01:56:51.170
AND LESS RESOURCE USE.

01:56:51.830 --> 01:56:56.480
BY PASSING AB 3059, WE'RE HOPING
TO CLOSE

01:56:56.480 --> 01:56:59.000
HEALTH DISPARITIES BEGINNING
AT BIRTH.

01:57:01.680 --> 01:57:02.160
&GT;&GT; SORRY.

01:57:02.220 --> 01:57:02.940
IT'S OKAY.

01:57:03.180 --> 01:57:06.270
DONOR MILK IS A COVERED BENEFIT
UNDER MEDI-CAL,

01:57:06.270 --> 01:57:09.450
BUT EXISTING LAW DOES NOT
CLEARLY DEFINE IT AS

01:57:09.450 --> 01:57:12.210
A COVERED BENEFIT UNDER
COMMERCIAL HEALTH PLANS.

01:57:12.570 --> 01:57:15.510
AB 3059 WOULD ENSURE PARITY AND
REQUIRE

01:57:15.510 --> 01:57:16.680
THAT ALL COMMERCIAL HEALTH

01:57:16.680 --> 01:57:18.390
PLANS PROVIDE COVERAGE FOR
MEDICALLY

01:57:18.390 --> 01:57:19.950
NECESSARY DONOR MILK.

01:57:20.220 --> 01:57:22.800
AB 3059 WOULD ALSO ADDRESS A
CHALLENGE

01:57:22.800 --> 01:57:25.260
TO ESTABLISHING A DONOR MILK
PROGRAM.

01:57:25.590 --> 01:57:28.020
ABOUT 12% OF NICUS IN CALIFORNIA

01:57:28.020 --> 01:57:29.520
DO NOT USE DONOR MILK,

01:57:29.520 --> 01:57:31.830
AND ONE OF THE MAIN BARRIERS TO
ESTABLISHING

01:57:31.830 --> 01:57:32.940
A DONOR MILK PROGRAM

01:57:32.940 --> 01:57:34.410
IS THE REQUIREMENT THAT
HOSPITALS

01:57:34.410 --> 01:57:35.550
OBTAIN A TISSUE BANK

01:57:35.550 --> 01:57:39.390
LICENSE IN ORDER TO STORE AND
DISTRIBUTE THIS MILK.

