ASSEMBLY MEMBER PELLERIN.

02:04:28.800 --> 02:04:30.990
HEALTH CARE COVERAGE, REVIEWS
AND GRIEVANCES.

02:04:30.990 --> 02:04:31.920
THANK YOU FOR JOINING US.

02:04:31.920 --> 02:04:33.210
PLEASE PROCEED WHEN READY.

02:04:33.240 --> 02:04:35.730
&GT;&GT; THANK YOU, CHAIR AND
SENATORS,

02:04:35.730 --> 02:04:38.700
I WOULD LIKE TO ACCEPT THE
COMMITTEE'S AMENDMENTS

02:04:38.700 --> 02:04:41.700
AND SINCERELY THANK THE
CONSULTANT FOR

02:04:41.700 --> 02:04:44.310
ALL OF HER HARD WORK ON THIS
BILL.

02:04:44.400 --> 02:04:47.460
FAR TOO OFTEN, CALIFORNIANS
DON'T RECEIVE THE CARE

02:04:47.460 --> 02:04:50.040
THEY NEED IN A TIMELY AND
APPROPRIATE MANNER,

02:04:50.040 --> 02:04:51.780
AND HEALTH PLANS AND INSURERS

02:04:51.780 --> 02:04:53.820
DO NOT CONSISTENTLY DECIDE OR

02:04:53.820 --> 02:04:55.290
PROVIDE PROPER NOTICE OF THEIR

02:04:55.290 --> 02:04:57.330
DECISIONS CONCERNING CLAIMS.

02:04:57.330 --> 02:04:59.130
THIS LEADS CONSUMERS TO BEAR

02:04:59.130 --> 02:05:00.780
THE FINANCIAL COSTS OF
PRESCRIBED

02:05:00.780 --> 02:05:02.340
CARE WHILE WAITING FOR A
RESPONSE

02:05:02.340 --> 02:05:03.420
FROM THEIR HEALTH PLAN,

02:05:03.420 --> 02:05:05.730
OR TO FOREGO TREATMENT
ALTOGETHER

02:05:05.730 --> 02:05:06.570
BECAUSE THEY CANNOT

02:05:06.570 --> 02:05:09.030
AFFORD TO PAY FOR THEIR CARE
OUT OF POCKET.

02:05:09.210 --> 02:05:11.850
THIS BILL ADDRESSES TWO PROBLEMS
FIRST,

02:05:11.850 --> 02:05:14.490
THE UNTIMELY RESOLUTION OF
CLAIMS AND GRIEVANCES

02:05:14.490 --> 02:05:16.620
BY HEALTH PLANS AND INSURERS,

02:05:16.620 --> 02:05:19.710
AND SECOND, A LACK OF
TRANSPARENCY IN DUE PROCESS.

02:05:19.710 --> 02:05:22.440
WHEN CONSUMERS FILE REGULATORY
COMPLAINTS.

02:05:22.500 --> 02:05:24.240
TO ADDRESS THE FIRST CONCERN,

02:05:24.240 --> 02:05:25.380
THIS BILL WILL HARMONIZE

02:05:25.380 --> 02:05:28.080
STATE LAW WITH FEDERAL LAW
REGARDING THE TIMELINE

02:05:28.080 --> 02:05:30.390
FOR RESPONDING TO CLAIMS FOR
COVERAGE AND HOW

02:05:30.390 --> 02:05:32.880
CLAIMS FOR URGENT CONDITIONS
ARE TREATED.

02:05:33.030 --> 02:05:35.670
THE BILL ALSO ADDS AN IMPORTANT
PROTECTION FOR THOSE

02:05:35.670 --> 02:05:38.070
WITH DEGENERATIVE CONDITIONS,
SUCH AS MS.,

02:05:38.070 --> 02:05:39.900
PRIORITIZING TREATMENT THAT CAN

02:05:39.900 --> 02:05:41.910
MINIMIZE THE LOSS OF FUNCTION,

02:05:41.910 --> 02:05:44.550
INSTEAD OF ONLY THOSE TREATMENTS
WHICH CAN

02:05:44.550 --> 02:05:47.190
RESTORE THE PATIENT TO FULL
FUNCTION.

02:05:47.190 --> 02:05:49.020
THIS ENSURES THAT THESE PATIENTS

02:05:49.020 --> 02:05:50.130
RECEIVE THE CARE THEY NEED,

02:05:50.130 --> 02:05:52.020
DESPITE THE FACT THAT THEY WILL
LIKELY

02:05:52.020 --> 02:05:54.030
NEVER RETURN TO FULL CARE.

02:05:54.030 --> 02:05:58.230
FULL HEALTH CARE DELAYED IS CARE
DENIED.

02:05:58.230 --> 02:06:00.480
THEREFORE, WHEN HEALTH PLANS
DON'T RESPOND

02:06:00.480 --> 02:06:02.760
TO REQUESTS FOR CARE IN A TIMELY
MANNER,

02:06:02.760 --> 02:06:04.680
THIS BILL PROVIDES AN INTERNAL

02:06:04.680 --> 02:06:06.090
GRIEVANCE WILL AUTOMATICALLY

02:06:06.090 --> 02:06:09.750
BE INITIATED INITIATED ON A
CONSUMER'S BEHALF.

02:06:09.750 --> 02:06:11.520
THE BILL THEN CLARIFIES

02:06:11.520 --> 02:06:12.870
THE TIMELINE AND NOTIFICATION

02:06:12.870 --> 02:06:14.460
REQUIREMENTS FOR GRIEVANCES,

02:06:14.460 --> 02:06:16.500
AGAIN BRINGING STATE LAW INTO

02:06:16.500 --> 02:06:18.210
ACCORDANCE WITH FEDERAL LAW.

02:06:18.300 --> 02:06:20.970
IF A HEALTH PLAN ALSO FAILS TO
RESPOND TO

02:06:20.970 --> 02:06:23.310
A GRIEVANCE WITHIN THE REQUIRED
TIMELINES,

02:06:23.310 --> 02:06:25.260
THAT GRIEVANCE WILL
AUTOMATICALLY

02:06:25.260 --> 02:06:27.570
RESOLVE IN FAVOR OF THE
CONSUMER,

02:06:27.570 --> 02:06:29.550
MEANING THEY CAN GET CARE WITH

02:06:29.550 --> 02:06:31.830
THE ASSURANCE THAT IT WILL BE
COVERED.

02:06:31.830 --> 02:06:34.530
THIS PROVISION FOLLOWS THE LEAD
OF 12 OTHER STATES,

02:06:34.530 --> 02:06:36.300
RANGING RANGING FROM ARKANSAS

02:06:36.300 --> 02:06:37.740
TO GEORGIA TO NEW YORK,

02:06:37.740 --> 02:06:39.840
WHICH HAVE EQUIVALENT
PROVISIONS.

02:06:39.840 --> 02:06:41.820
THIS DOES NOT APPLY IN THE CASE
OF

02:06:41.820 --> 02:06:43.290
INCOMPLETE GRIEVANCE REQUESTS,

02:06:43.290 --> 02:06:45.720
OR WHERE A REQUEST IS FOR
EXPERIMENTAL TREATMENT,

02:06:45.720 --> 02:06:47.940
WHERE MORE RESEARCH MAY BE
NEEDED.

02:06:48.000 --> 02:06:50.790
LAST YEAR, DMHC FOUND THAT OUR
STATE'S

02:06:50.790 --> 02:06:52.560
LARGEST HEALTH PLAN HAD FAILED
TO

02:06:52.560 --> 02:06:54.660
RESOLVE TENS OF THOUSANDS OF
GRIEVANCES

02:06:54.660 --> 02:06:56.640
WITHIN THE REQUIRED TIME FRAME.

02:06:56.640 --> 02:06:59.130
THIS BILL PROVIDES A STRONG
INCENTIVE FOR THESE

02:06:59.130 --> 02:07:01.470
DISPUTES TO BE RESOLVED IN A
TIMELY MANNER,

02:07:01.470 --> 02:07:03.060
REDUCING THE LIKELIHOOD THAT

02:07:03.060 --> 02:07:04.710
PATIENT CONDITIONS WORSEN

02:07:04.710 --> 02:07:07.050
AND SUBSEQUENTLY REQUIRE MORE
INTENSIVE

02:07:07.050 --> 02:07:08.340
AND COSTLY TREATMENT.

02:07:08.340 --> 02:07:10.830
WHILE THEY ARE STUCK IN LIMBO
WAITING

02:07:10.830 --> 02:07:12.480
FOR A HEALTH PLAN RESPONSE.

02:07:12.750 --> 02:07:14.490
TO ADDRESS THE SECOND CONCERN,

02:07:14.520 --> 02:07:15.690
THE LACK OF TRANSPARENCY

02:07:15.690 --> 02:07:18.030
AND DUE PROCESS IN REGULATORY
COMPLAINTS,

02:07:18.030 --> 02:07:19.830
THIS BILL REQUIRES THAT PLANS

02:07:19.830 --> 02:07:21.660
OR INSURERS OFFER COPIES OF

02:07:21.660 --> 02:07:23.640
ALL COMMUNICATIONS WITH DMHC

02:07:23.670 --> 02:07:25.680
TO THE ENROLLEE OR INSURED,

02:07:25.680 --> 02:07:27.990
AND PROMPTLY PROVIDE THOSE
RECORDS

02:07:27.990 --> 02:07:30.540
IF THE ENROLLEE OR INSURED WANTS
THEM.

02:07:30.870 --> 02:07:33.540
AB 3260 WILL IMPROVE
TRANSPARENCY BY

02:07:33.540 --> 02:07:35.220
ALLOWING THE CONSUMER TO KNOW
WHAT

02:07:35.220 --> 02:07:36.930
INFORMATION HAS BEEN SUBMITTED
TO

02:07:36.930 --> 02:07:39.270
THE PLAN SHOULD THEY SO DESIRE.

02:07:39.540 --> 02:07:42.210
UNFORTUNATELY, THE CURRENT
REALITY AROUND

02:07:42.210 --> 02:07:44.580
COMPLAINTS DISADVANTAGES
CONSUMERS

02:07:44.580 --> 02:07:46.620
WHO SEE OR HEAR LITTLE WHILE
THEIR

02:07:46.620 --> 02:07:48.330
COMPLAINT IS BEING REVIEWED.

02:07:48.330 --> 02:07:51.570
HEALTH PLANS AND INSURERS, ON
THE OTHER HAND,

02:07:51.570 --> 02:07:53.520
ENJOY FREQUENT AND REGULAR
COMMUNICATION

02:07:53.520 --> 02:07:54.810
WITH REGULATORS.

02:07:54.810 --> 02:07:57.090
WHILE HEALTH PLANS FAIL TO
FOLLOW THE LAW,

02:07:57.090 --> 02:07:59.700
CONSUMERS SUFFER THE
CONSEQUENCES.

02:07:59.700 --> 02:08:02.220
THESE COSTS FALL PARTICULARLY
HARD

02:08:02.220 --> 02:08:03.630
ON UNDERSERVED COMMUNITIES,

02:08:03.630 --> 02:08:06.120
WHERE PATIENTS CANNOT AFFORD
TO PAY CARE

02:08:06.120 --> 02:08:08.310
FOR CARE OUT OF POCKET WHILE
THEY WAIT

02:08:08.310 --> 02:08:09.780
FOR HEALTH PLANS TO RESPOND
TO THEIR

02:08:09.780 --> 02:08:12.420
CLAIMS OR RESOLVE THEIR
GRIEVANCES.

02:08:12.420 --> 02:08:15.120
TAXPAYERS IN OUR COUNTIES ALSO
BEAR A COST,

02:08:15.120 --> 02:08:18.300
BECAUSE MANY OF THESE SAME
PATIENTS WILL SEEK

02:08:18.300 --> 02:08:20.880
CARE FROM PUBLIC SERVICES IN
THE MEANTIME,

02:08:21.330 --> 02:08:23.640
AB 3260 HAS ENJOYED BIPARTISAN

02:08:23.640 --> 02:08:24.600
SUPPORT BECAUSE IT WILL

02:08:24.600 --> 02:08:28.710
IMPROVE PROCESSES FOR ALL
MEDICAL SURGICAL ISSUES.

02:08:28.710 --> 02:08:30.870
I'M ESPECIALLY EAGER TO SEE THE
IMPROVEMENTS

02:08:30.870 --> 02:08:32.130
THIS MEASURE WILL MAKE FOR THOSE

02:08:32.130 --> 02:08:33.990
SEEKING TREATMENT FOR BEHAVIORAL
HEALTH

02:08:33.990 --> 02:08:35.760
AND SUBSTANCE USE DISORDERS,

02:08:35.760 --> 02:08:38.220
AS THESE ARE AMONG THE AREAS
WHERE PATIENTS STRUGGLE

02:08:38.220 --> 02:08:41.010
MOST TO GET TIMELY AND
APPROPRIATE CARE.

02:08:41.040 --> 02:08:44.370
WITH ME TO TESTIFY IN SUPPORT
OF AB 3260

02:08:44.370 --> 02:08:48.060
IS DOCTOR KARIN SACCO AND LAUREN
FINK.

02:08:48.150 --> 02:08:50.100
LAUREN FINK IS THE SENIOR
DIRECTOR

02:08:50.100 --> 02:08:52.290
OF POLICY FOR THE KENNEDY FORUM.

02:08:52.290 --> 02:08:54.030
BENJAMIN ECKERT FROM THE
NATIONAL

02:08:54.030 --> 02:08:54.840
UNION OF HEALTH CARE

02:08:54.840 --> 02:08:57.630
WORKERS IS ALSO HERE FOR ANY
TECHNICAL QUESTIONS.

02:08:58.530 --> 02:08:59.250
WELCOME.

02:08:59.250 --> 02:09:00.210
THANK YOU FOR JOINING US.

02:09:00.210 --> 02:09:02.370
PLEASE IDENTIFY YOURSELVES FOR
THE RECORD.

02:09:02.370 --> 02:09:03.510
BEFORE YOU SPEAK.

02:09:03.510 --> 02:09:05.280
I'LL LET YOU DECIDE WHO MOVES
FIRST.

02:09:05.280 --> 02:09:06.810
AND REMEMBER, WE HAVE ABOUT

02:09:06.810 --> 02:09:09.240
SIX MINUTES FOR THE SIDE.

02:09:09.240 --> 02:09:09.570
&GT;&GT; OKAY.

02:09:09.960 --> 02:09:11.820
GOOD AFTERNOON, CHAIR AND
COMMITTEE MEMBERS.

02:09:11.820 --> 02:09:14.070
I'M DOCTOR KARIN MCINTOSH SACCO.

02:09:14.100 --> 02:09:16.830
I AM A DUAL LICENSED MENTAL
HEALTH PROFESSIONAL.

02:09:16.830 --> 02:09:18.840
I'M LICENSED AS BOTH A MARRIAGE
AND FAMILY

02:09:18.840 --> 02:09:21.180
THERAPIST AND AS A PSYCHOLOGIST.

02:09:21.180 --> 02:09:22.470
I HAVE OVER 20 YEARS.

02:09:22.590 --> 02:09:24.180
OF EXPERIENCE HELPING PEOPLE
WITH

02:09:24.180 --> 02:09:26.070
A RANGE OF PRESENTING ISSUES,

02:09:26.070 --> 02:09:29.160
FROM SITUATIONAL STRESSORS TO
SEVERE

02:09:29.160 --> 02:09:30.450
MENTAL HEALTH CONCERNS.

02:09:30.450 --> 02:09:33.210
AND I'VE WORKED IN A VARIETY
OF SETTINGS,

02:09:33.210 --> 02:09:34.440
INCLUDING SCHOOLS,

02:09:34.440 --> 02:09:36.060
COMMUNITY MENTAL HEALTH CENTERS,

02:09:36.060 --> 02:09:37.860
GROUP HOMES, AND INTENSIVE
OUTPATIENT

02:09:37.890 --> 02:09:39.090
TREATMENT PROGRAMS.

02:09:39.120 --> 02:09:42.150
I CURRENTLY PROVIDE DIRECT
CLINICAL SERVICES TO

02:09:42.150 --> 02:09:44.850
CALIFORNIA RESIDENTS IN MY
OUTPATIENT PRACTICE.

02:09:45.090 --> 02:09:46.500
THERE HAVE BEEN TIMES IN WHICH

02:09:46.530 --> 02:09:48.000
MY PROFESSIONAL TRAINING

02:09:48.000 --> 02:09:50.910
AND EXPERTISE LEAD ME TO
DETERMINE THAT A CLIENT

02:09:50.910 --> 02:09:53.700
I'M SERVING MAY NEED A HIGHER
LEVEL OF CARE THAN MY

02:09:53.700 --> 02:09:56.940
OUTPATIENT PRACTICE CAN PROVIDE,
IN SOME CASES,

02:09:56.940 --> 02:09:58.740
ONCE OR TWICE WEEKLY OUTPATIENT

02:09:58.740 --> 02:10:00.030
THERAPY DOES NOT PROVIDE

02:10:00.030 --> 02:10:02.130
THE CARE NEEDED TO MANAGE SEVERE

02:10:02.130 --> 02:10:03.600
MENTAL HEALTH SYMPTOMS,

02:10:03.600 --> 02:10:06.420
AND WHEN THIS HAPPENS,
TRANSITIONING TO THAT HIGHER

02:10:06.420 --> 02:10:09.840
LEVEL OF CARE IS URGENT AND
MEDICALLY NECESSARY.

02:10:09.840 --> 02:10:11.970
WHEN SOMEONE IS MEETING CRITERIA
FOR

02:10:11.970 --> 02:10:13.620
THIS ESCALATION OF TREATMENT,

02:10:13.620 --> 02:10:15.750
THEY ARE OFTEN DEBILITATED BY
THEIR MENTAL

02:10:15.750 --> 02:10:19.020
HEALTH SYMPTOMS SUCH AS MOOD
INSTABILITY,

02:10:19.020 --> 02:10:22.860
ISOLATION, TEARFULNESS, SLEEP
DISTURBANCE,

02:10:22.860 --> 02:10:25.560
HOPELESSNESS, LOSS OF INTEREST,

02:10:25.560 --> 02:10:30.720
PANIC ATTACKS, INTENSE FEAR, AND
SUICIDAL IDEATION.

02:10:31.140 --> 02:10:33.060
THEIR FUNCTIONING BECOMES
MODERATELY

02:10:33.060 --> 02:10:34.020
TO SIGNIFICANTLY

02:10:34.020 --> 02:10:36.180
IMPAIRED DUE TO THEIR MENTAL
HEALTH SYMPTOMS,

02:10:36.180 --> 02:10:38.040
AND THEY EXPERIENCE A
DETERIORATION

02:10:38.040 --> 02:10:38.850
IN THEIR PERFORMANCE

02:10:38.850 --> 02:10:42.720
OF RESPONSIBILITIES AT HOME,
SCHOOL, AND OR WORK.

02:10:43.420 --> 02:10:46.000
DUE TO THE SIGNIFICANT EMOTIONAL
DISTRESS

02:10:46.000 --> 02:10:47.860
SOMEONE IS EXPERIENCING AT THE
TIME,

02:10:47.860 --> 02:10:50.440
A RECOMMENDATION FOR A HIGHER
LEVEL OF CARE IS MADE.

02:10:50.440 --> 02:10:53.380
IT'S ONLY MADE WORSE WHEN THEIR
HEALTH PLAN FAILS TO

02:10:53.380 --> 02:10:56.050
AUTHORIZE THE REFERRAL FOR A
HIGHER LEVEL OF CARE,

02:10:56.050 --> 02:10:59.620
OR WORSE, FAILS TO RESPOND TO
THAT REFERRAL AT ALL.

02:11:00.190 --> 02:11:03.310
I HAVE WITNESSED MANY CLIENTS
LANGUISH OR EXPERIENCE

02:11:03.310 --> 02:11:06.100
AN EXACERBATION OF THEIR ALREADY
HEIGHTENED

02:11:06.100 --> 02:11:08.920
EMOTIONAL DISTRESS DUE TO
ATTEMPTING TO NAVIGATE

02:11:08.920 --> 02:11:11.110
THEIR HEALTH PLANS REFERRAL
SYSTEM,

02:11:11.110 --> 02:11:13.030
ONLY TO LEARN THAT THEIR HEALTH
PLAN HAS

02:11:13.030 --> 02:11:15.310
NOT PROCESSED THE REFERRAL OR
WORSE,

02:11:15.310 --> 02:11:17.050
HAS DENIED THE REFERRAL FOR
CARE.

02:11:17.900 --> 02:11:21.230
AB 3260 WOULD ALLEVIATE THE
UNDUE HARDSHIP

02:11:21.230 --> 02:11:22.850
FOR CONSUMERS BY REQUIRING

02:11:22.850 --> 02:11:25.790
HEALTH PLANS TO INITIATE A
GRIEVANCE ON A CONSUMER'S

02:11:25.790 --> 02:11:27.710
BEHALF WHEN THEY FAIL TO RESPOND

02:11:27.710 --> 02:11:28.790
TO CLAIMS WITHIN THE TIME

02:11:28.790 --> 02:11:31.730
PERIOD AND IN THE MANNER
REQUIRED BY EXISTING LAW.

02:11:32.090 --> 02:11:34.280
AB 3260 WOULD ALSO REQUIRE
HEALTH

02:11:34.280 --> 02:11:36.170
PLANS AND DISABILITY INSURERS

02:11:36.170 --> 02:11:38.180
TO AUTOMATICALLY RESOLVE
GRIEVANCES

02:11:38.180 --> 02:11:39.680
IN FAVOR OF THE CONSUMER

02:11:39.680 --> 02:11:41.600
IF THEY DO NOT RESPOND WITHIN

02:11:41.600 --> 02:11:43.400
THE LEGALLY REQUIRED TIME FRAME,

02:11:43.400 --> 02:11:45.410
72 HOURS FOR URGENT CASES

02:11:45.410 --> 02:11:47.690
AND 30 DAYS FOR NON URGENT
CASES.

02:11:47.960 --> 02:11:50.240
THE AUTOMATIC INITIATION OF
AGREEMENTS WOULD

02:11:50.240 --> 02:11:52.430
BE LIFE CHANGING FOR MANY
INDIVIDUALS,

02:11:52.430 --> 02:11:54.890
AS CURRENTLY THIS RESPONSIBILITY
FALLS ON

02:11:54.890 --> 02:11:57.320
THEM AND MANY DON'T HAVE THE
ENERGY OR

02:11:57.320 --> 02:12:00.110
THE MENTAL CAPACITY REQUIRED TO
NAVIGATE THIS

02:12:00.110 --> 02:12:02.510
ADMINISTRATIVE AND BUREAUCRATIC
PROCESS,

02:12:02.510 --> 02:12:04.610
ESPECIALLY AT A TIME WHEN
THEY'RE DEBILITATED

02:12:04.610 --> 02:12:06.200
BY THEIR MENTAL HEALTH SYMPTOMS.

02:12:06.590 --> 02:12:10.850
ULTIMATELY, AB 3260, IN PRACTICE
TRANSLATES

02:12:10.850 --> 02:12:12.260
TO CALIFORNIA RESIDENTS

02:12:12.260 --> 02:12:13.730
RECEIVING THE LEVEL OF CARE

02:12:13.730 --> 02:12:15.260
THEY NEED AND THEY DESERVE.

02:12:15.590 --> 02:12:16.280
THANK YOU.

02:12:16.310 --> 02:12:17.210
THANK YOU.

02:12:17.240 --> 02:12:18.230
NEXT, PLEASE.

02:12:18.230 --> 02:12:18.440
MR..

02:12:19.530 --> 02:12:20.730
&GT;&GT; THANK YOU, CHAIR AND MEMBERS.

02:12:20.730 --> 02:12:21.510
I'M LAUREN FINK,

02:12:21.540 --> 02:12:24.420
SENIOR DIRECTOR OF POLICY AT THE
KENNEDY FORUM.

02:12:24.420 --> 02:12:26.880
WE'RE PROUD CO-SPONSORS OF AB
3260.

02:12:26.910 --> 02:12:29.610
CALIFORNIA HAS ROBUST CONSUMER
PROTECTIONS

02:12:29.610 --> 02:12:31.110
FOR MENTAL HEALTH AND ADDICTION
CARE,

02:12:31.110 --> 02:12:33.900
BOTH IN SB 855 GROUNDBREAKING
PARITY LAWS

02:12:33.900 --> 02:12:36.960
AND AN SB 221 TIMELY ACCESS
PROTECTIONS.

02:12:36.990 --> 02:12:38.850
WHILE THESE LAWS ARE CLEAR AND
ROBUST,

02:12:38.850 --> 02:12:39.630
THEY ARE PROTECTIVE.

02:12:39.630 --> 02:12:41.730
STRENGTH IS DEPENDENT ON PLAN
COMPLIANCE

02:12:41.730 --> 02:12:43.470
AND REGULATOR ENFORCEMENT.

02:12:43.620 --> 02:12:46.590
AB 3260 STRENGTHENS PROTECTIONS
FOR PATIENTS

02:12:46.590 --> 02:12:48.720
FACING DELAYS OR DENIALS IN
CARE,

02:12:48.720 --> 02:12:50.910
ENSURING HEALTH PLANS ADHERE
TO STATE LAWS

02:12:50.940 --> 02:12:52.680
AND THAT REGULATORS ENFORCE
THEM.

02:12:52.860 --> 02:12:54.600
AS WE'VE HEARD FROM MY COLLEAGUE
TODAY,

02:12:54.600 --> 02:12:55.950
COMMERCIALLY INSURED PATIENTS

02:12:55.950 --> 02:12:57.810
OFTEN FACE DELAYS OR DENIALS

02:12:57.810 --> 02:12:59.880
WHEN SEEKING MENTAL HEALTH AND
ADDICTION CARE.

02:12:59.910 --> 02:13:02.880
HEALTH PLANS REGULARLY FAIL TO
APPROVE CARE WITHIN

02:13:02.880 --> 02:13:05.640
LEGAL TIMELINES OR UNJUSTLY DENY
COVERAGE,

02:13:05.640 --> 02:13:07.530
ALTHOUGH PATIENTS CAN SEEK
RECOURSE.

02:13:07.530 --> 02:13:09.540
THAT PROCESS IS SLOW, OPAQUE,

02:13:09.540 --> 02:13:12.300
AND OFTEN RESULTS IN DELAYED OR
DENIED TREATMENT.

02:13:12.630 --> 02:13:15.360
THE TYPICAL PROCESS INVOLVES A
PATIENT OR PROVIDER

02:13:15.360 --> 02:13:17.550
REQUESTING AUTHORIZATION FROM
THE HEALTH PLAN.

02:13:17.550 --> 02:13:19.770
IF DENIED, PATIENTS CAN FILE
AN INTERNAL

02:13:19.770 --> 02:13:21.000
GRIEVANCE WITH THEIR PLAN,

02:13:21.000 --> 02:13:22.350
AND IF THAT FAILS, THEY CAN
ISSUE

02:13:22.350 --> 02:13:23.940
A COMPLAINT WITH REGULATORS.

02:13:24.000 --> 02:13:25.890
WHEN HEALTH PLANS DO NOT COMPLY
WITH LEGAL

02:13:25.890 --> 02:13:27.930
TIMELINES AND NOTIFICATION
REQUIREMENTS,

02:13:27.930 --> 02:13:29.610
PATIENTS GET STUCK IN LIMBO
WAITING

