IMPACT OF TOXIC

02:24:23.050 --> 02:24:24.730
CHEMICAL EXPOSURES ON OUR
PATIENTS,

02:24:24.730 --> 02:24:26.260
PARTICULARLY THOSE FROM
VULNERABLE

02:24:26.260 --> 02:24:28.060
COMMUNITIES IN RURAL HOSPITALS.

02:24:28.480 --> 02:24:30.640
USING DEHP FREE MEDICAL DEVICES

02:24:30.640 --> 02:24:32.320
IS NOT JUST A MATTER OF SAFETY,

02:24:32.320 --> 02:24:34.000
IT'S A MATTER OF HEALTH EQUITY.

02:24:34.120 --> 02:24:37.330
BY CONTINUING TO USE DEHP
CONTAINING IV BAGS,

02:24:37.330 --> 02:24:39.850
WE ARE EXACERBATING EXISTING
HEALTH DISPARITIES

02:24:39.850 --> 02:24:42.820
AND PUTTING OUR PATIENTS AT
UNNECESSARY RISK.

02:24:42.850 --> 02:24:44.980
TRANSITIONING TO SAFER
ALTERNATIVES

02:24:44.980 --> 02:24:46.300
NOW IS CRUCIAL FOR

02:24:46.300 --> 02:24:48.640
PROTECTING THE HEALTH AND LIVES
OF ALL PATIENTS,

02:24:48.640 --> 02:24:51.280
ESPECIALLY THOSE WHO ARE ALREADY
AT A HIGHER RISK.

02:24:51.459 --> 02:24:54.250
WE RESPECTFULLY ASK FOR AN I
VOTE AND OPPOSE ANY

02:24:54.250 --> 02:24:56.709
UNNECESSARY DELAYS IN ITS
IMPLEMENTATION.

02:24:56.709 --> 02:25:00.250
ENSURING THE TIMELY PHASEOUT OF
DEHP WILL PROTECT

02:25:00.250 --> 02:25:01.959
VULNERABLE POPULATIONS FROM
