NEGATIVE IMPACTS

02:25:42.100 --> 02:25:44.020
IT CAN HAVE ON THE DEVELOPING
FETUS.

02:25:44.530 --> 02:25:46.000
ACCORDING TO THE CDC,

02:25:46.150 --> 02:25:49.450
EXPOSURE DURING PREGNANCY MAY
LEAD TO PRETERM BIRTH.

02:25:51.870 --> 02:25:54.090
DELAYED MENTAL HEALTH
DEVELOPMENT AND ALTERED

02:25:54.120 --> 02:25:55.860
TIMING OF PUBERTY IN THE CHILD.

02:25:55.860 --> 02:25:57.840
STUDIES OUT OF HARVARD HAD
DEMONSTRATED

02:25:57.840 --> 02:25:59.550
THAT PATIENTS WITH HIGHER LEVELS

02:25:59.550 --> 02:26:01.890
