03:09:26.930 --> 03:09:27.440
MR.

03:09:27.440 --> 03:09:28.760
CHAIR AND MEMBERS, MY NAME.

03:09:28.760 --> 03:09:29.629
IS LISA LUM.

03:09:29.629 --> 03:09:31.040
THANK YOU FOR LETTING ME SPEAK
TODAY

03:09:31.040 --> 03:09:32.510
ON BEHALF OF MY SON TREVOR,

03:09:32.510 --> 03:09:34.310
WHO WAS DIAGNOSED WITH CROHN'S
DISEASE

03:09:34.310 --> 03:09:36.410
TWO YEARS AGO AT THE AGE OF
NINE.

03:09:36.950 --> 03:09:39.170
ON NOVEMBER 1ST, 2022,

03:09:39.170 --> 03:09:41.090
TREVOR WAS PLACED ON REMICADE.

03:09:41.120 --> 03:09:44.120
OUR INSURANCE APPROVED THE FIRST
THREE INFUSIONS,

03:09:44.120 --> 03:09:46.040
WHICH WERE ONLY A FEW WEEKS
APART,

03:09:46.040 --> 03:09:47.900
FOLLOWED BY A MAINTENANCE
INFUSION

03:09:47.900 --> 03:09:49.129
EVERY EIGHT WEEKS.

03:09:49.129 --> 03:09:51.470
WITHIN THOSE FIRST WEEKS, WE
WERE EXCITED

03:09:51.470 --> 03:09:53.390
TO SEE IMPROVEMENT IN HIS
CONDITION,

03:09:53.390 --> 03:09:55.070
SHOWING MINIMAL BLEEDING.

03:09:55.160 --> 03:09:57.290
THIS HADN'T HAPPENED SINCE HE
BEGAN SYMPTOMS

03:09:57.290 --> 03:09:58.910
IN MARCH EARLIER THAT YEAR.

03:09:58.940 --> 03:10:00.530
ALTHOUGH WE SAW PROGRESS,

03:10:00.530 --> 03:10:02.330
TREVOR DID NOT HAVE THE OPTIMAL
LEVELS

03:10:02.330 --> 03:10:05.000
OF REMICADE IN HIS SYSTEM AFTER
THE THIRD INFUSION,

03:10:05.000 --> 03:10:07.430
SO THE DOCTOR REQUESTED TO
CHANGE MAINTENANCE

03:10:07.430 --> 03:10:09.590
FROM EVERY EIGHT WEEKS TO EVERY
FOUR.

03:10:10.070 --> 03:10:12.890
ON DECEMBER 20TH, THE FIRST
INSURANCE DENIAL

03:10:12.890 --> 03:10:15.050
STATED LACK OF MEDICAL
NECESSITY.

03:10:15.050 --> 03:10:17.570
HIS DOCTOR APPEALED, RESUBMITTED
CLINICAL

03:10:17.570 --> 03:10:19.820
TRIALS TO SUPPORT HER HER
REQUEST,

03:10:19.820 --> 03:10:21.620
AND ASKED FOR AN EXPEDITED
REVIEW,

03:10:21.620 --> 03:10:23.000
WHICH WAS ALSO DENIED.

03:10:23.390 --> 03:10:26.180
ON JANUARY 21ST, A SECOND DENIAL
CAME,

03:10:26.180 --> 03:10:27.020
STATING AGAIN,

03:10:27.020 --> 03:10:29.330
LACK OF MEDICAL NECESSITY EVEN

03:10:29.330 --> 03:10:30.740
AFTER MULTIPLE PHONE CALLS,

03:10:30.740 --> 03:10:32.270
EMAILS AND SUBMITTED DOCUMENTS

03:10:32.270 --> 03:10:33.800
FROM THE DOCTOR AND MYSELF.

03:10:33.800 --> 03:10:36.680
THIS WAS NOW SIX WEEKS AFTER
TREVOR'S LAST INFUSION,

03:10:36.680 --> 03:10:38.060
AND HE HAD BEEN HOME FROM SCHOOL

03:10:38.060 --> 03:10:40.010
WITH INCREASED BLOODY STOOLS

03:10:40.010 --> 03:10:41.510
AND HAD TO START ON STEROIDS

03:10:41.510 --> 03:10:42.709
BECAUSE OF ALL THE WAITING.

03:10:43.430 --> 03:10:45.080
WE MADE A THIRD AND LAST ATTEMPT

03:10:45.080 --> 03:10:46.100
TO ASK FOR AN INCREASED

03:10:46.100 --> 03:10:48.050
DOSAGE AMOUNT AT THE EIGHT WEEK
INFUSION,

03:10:48.050 --> 03:10:51.110
AND AGAIN DENIED ON JANUARY
25TH.

03:10:51.140 --> 03:10:52.850
I SUBMITTED AN INDEPENDENT
MEDICAL

03:10:52.850 --> 03:10:53.870
REVIEW COMPLAINT TO

03:10:53.870 --> 03:10:55.129
THE DEPARTMENT OF MANAGED HEALTH

03:10:55.129 --> 03:10:57.350
CARE ON JANUARY 28TH.

03:10:57.350 --> 03:11:00.650
AFTER JUST TWO DAYS OF THE
DEPARTMENT'S INVOLVEMENT,

03:11:00.650 --> 03:11:02.209
THE INSURANCE FINALLY APPROVED

03:11:02.209 --> 03:11:03.620
THE FOUR WEEK INTERVAL DOSE,

03:11:03.620 --> 03:11:06.379
ADMITTING THAT IT WAS INDEED A
MEDICAL NECESSITY

03:11:06.379 --> 03:11:09.379
AND TREVOR IS NOW RECEIVING A
DOSE EVERY FOUR WEEKS.

03:11:09.560 --> 03:11:11.600
THIS WAS A VERY EMOTIONAL AND
FRUSTRATING

03:11:11.629 --> 03:11:12.740
TIME IN OUR LIVES.

03:11:12.740 --> 03:11:14.959
SEEING OUR YOUNG SON IN PAIN
AND BLEEDING.

03:11:14.959 --> 03:11:16.520
WE WERE WORRIED, DESPERATE AND
AT

03:11:16.520 --> 03:11:18.470
THE MERCY OF THE INSURANCE
COMPANY.

03:11:18.500 --> 03:11:20.150
WE WERE ON THE EDGE OF OUR
SEATS,

03:11:20.150 --> 03:11:22.340
HOPING JUST FOR THE OPPORTUNITY,

03:11:22.340 --> 03:11:24.290
THAT ONE OF THE LIMITED
MEDICATIONS

03:11:24.290 --> 03:11:26.450
AVAILABLE FOR HIS AGE WOULD
WORK.

03:11:26.480 --> 03:11:29.420
LUCKILY, I'M A STAY AT HOME
MOTHER AND COULD DEVOTE

03:11:29.420 --> 03:11:32.720
MY TIME TO THIS EXHAUSTING
SITUATION IF HIS MEDICAL

03:11:32.720 --> 03:11:36.110
TEAM AND I DIDN'T ADVOCATE SO
FIERCELY FOR TREVOR,

03:11:36.110 --> 03:11:38.540
I DON'T KNOW HOW MUCH LONGER HE
WOULD HAVE SUFFERED.

03:11:38.540 --> 03:11:41.060
SO I'M HERE TODAY HOPING
TREVOR'S STORY COULD

03:11:41.060 --> 03:11:42.680
PROVIDE ANOTHER PERSPECTIVE
ON THIS

03:11:42.680 --> 03:11:44.600
MATTER AND COULD MAKE A
DIFFERENCE IN FORWARDING

03:11:44.600 --> 03:11:46.190
THE TREATMENT OF THIS DISEASE.

03:11:46.220 --> 03:11:47.000
THANK YOU.

03:11:47.030 --> 03:11:48.410
THANK YOU FOR COMING AND THANK
YOU

03:11:48.410 --> 03:11:49.970
FOR SHARING YOUR STORY, MA'AM.

03:11:53.060 --> 03:11:53.450
THANK YOU.

03:11:53.450 --> 03:11:53.990
BRIAN SPENCER.

03:11:53.990 --> 03:11:55.790
ON BEHALF OF THE CROHN'S AND
COLITIS FOUNDATION,

03:11:55.790 --> 03:11:58.250
THE SPONSORS OF AB 2169,

03:11:58.250 --> 03:12:00.140
I JUST WANT TO EMPHASIZE A FEW
THINGS.

03:12:00.140 --> 03:12:03.650
ONE, FIRST OF ALL IS AB 2169 IS
A MUCH MORE NARROWED

03:12:03.650 --> 03:12:05.870
SURGICAL APPROACH TO THIS ISSUE
THAN YOU'VE

03:12:05.870 --> 03:12:08.600
SEEN AND APPROVED IN PREVIOUS
YEARS IS SPECIFIC

03:12:08.600 --> 03:12:11.209
TO CHRONIC CONDITIONS AND CANCER
ONLY.

03:12:11.209 --> 03:12:12.440
IT DOES NOT APPLY TO OPIOIDS

03:12:12.440 --> 03:12:13.940
OR CONTROLLED SUBSTANCES

03:12:13.940 --> 03:12:15.980
AND IS LIMITED TO TWO DOSE
ESCALATIONS.

03:12:15.980 --> 03:12:17.720
AS WAS STATED, THERE WILL BE
COMMENTS BY

03:12:17.720 --> 03:12:20.360
THE OPPOSITION OF THE ISSUE OF
PATIENT SAFETY,

03:12:20.360 --> 03:12:22.190
BUT I CAN TELL YOU WHAT IS NOT
SAFE,

03:12:22.190 --> 03:12:23.450
AND THAT'S MOVING A PATIENT OFF

03:12:23.450 --> 03:12:25.190
OF A DRUG THAT WE KNOW WORKS.

03:12:25.190 --> 03:12:26.660
AND THE PATIENT WAS STABLE.

03:12:26.660 --> 03:12:28.760
THE REALITY IS THERE'S A LIMITED
SUPPLY OF

03:12:28.760 --> 03:12:30.950
DRUGS AVAILABLE THAT MAY OR MAY
NOT WORK.

03:12:30.950 --> 03:12:32.750
SO IT'S IMPERATIVE THAT
PROVIDERS ARE ABLE

03:12:32.750 --> 03:12:35.090
TO OPTIMIZE THE ONE DRUG THAT
DOES.

03:12:35.090 --> 03:12:36.709
IT'S NOT SOME EXPERIMENTAL DRUG

03:12:36.709 --> 03:12:38.270
THAT THE PLAN HAS NEVER SEEN.

03:12:38.270 --> 03:12:40.070
IT'S A DRUG THAT THEY HAVE
CURRENT

03:12:40.070 --> 03:12:41.450
THAT THEY ARE CURRENTLY COVERING

03:12:41.450 --> 03:12:43.340
AND CURRENTLY PRESCRIBED BY THE
PROVIDER,

03:12:43.340 --> 03:12:44.780
WHO ALONG WITH THE PATIENT,

03:12:44.780 --> 03:12:46.280
KNOW WHAT IS THE BEST CARE,

03:12:46.280 --> 03:12:47.930
IS A COMMON SENSE MEASURE THAT

03:12:47.930 --> 03:12:50.390
WILL HELP SO MANY PEOPLE, YOUNG
PEOPLE LIKE TREVOR.

03:12:50.420 --> 03:12:51.350
I ASK FOR YOUR VOTE.

