03:22:49.480 --> 03:22:51.040
PLEASED TO PRESENT THIS BILL,

03:22:51.040 --> 03:22:52.090
WHICH IS GOING TO BRING GREATER

03:22:52.090 --> 03:22:53.410
TRANSPARENCY IN THE WAY THAT

03:22:53.410 --> 03:22:55.060
THE CALIFORNIA DEPARTMENT OF
PUBLIC HEALTH

03:22:55.060 --> 03:22:56.560
RESPONSE TO COMPLAINTS REGARDING

03:22:56.560 --> 03:22:58.840
THE VIOLATION OF CALIFORNIA'S

03:22:58.870 --> 03:23:00.730
NURSE TO PATIENT RATIO LAW.

03:23:01.120 --> 03:23:02.590
AS YOU MAY KNOW, SINCE THE
PASSAGE

03:23:02.590 --> 03:23:04.060
OF KEY STAFFING RATIO LAWS,

03:23:04.090 --> 03:23:05.320
CALIFORNIA DEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC

03:23:05.320 --> 03:23:06.910
HEALTH HAS HELD THE IMPORTANT

03:23:06.910 --> 03:23:09.160
RESPONSIBILITY OF ENFORCING
THESE

03:23:09.160 --> 03:23:10.810
NURSE TO PATIENT RATIOS.

03:23:10.810 --> 03:23:12.190
DESPITE THE LAWS ON THE BOOKS,

03:23:12.190 --> 03:23:14.530
NURSES HAVE PERSISTENTLY RAISED
CONCERNS

03:23:14.530 --> 03:23:16.240
ABOUT CONTINUOUS VIOLATIONS OF

03:23:16.240 --> 03:23:18.250
THE LAW WITHIN THEIR WORKPLACES.

03:23:18.250 --> 03:23:19.870
THESE CONCERNS HAVE BEEN
CAREFULLY

03:23:19.870 --> 03:23:21.250
DOCUMENTED THROUGH

03:23:21.250 --> 03:23:22.600
THE SUBMISSION OF THOUSANDS OF

03:23:22.600 --> 03:23:24.670
STAFFING COMPLAINTS TO CDPH.

03:23:25.240 --> 03:23:28.000
THIS BILL WILL SUPPORT WORKPLACE
SAFETY EFFORTS

03:23:28.000 --> 03:23:31.090
AND IMPROVE TRANSPARENCY BY
REQUIRING CDPH

03:23:31.120 --> 03:23:33.520
TO CONCURRENTLY NOTIFY BOTH THE
HOSPITAL

03:23:33.520 --> 03:23:36.129
AND THE INDIVIDUAL WHO REPORTED
THE VIOLATION,

03:23:36.129 --> 03:23:37.900
ALONG WITH THEIR COLLECTIVE
BARGAINING

03:23:37.900 --> 03:23:39.340
AGENT OR REPRESENTATIVE,

03:23:39.340 --> 03:23:41.290
REGARDING THE ACTION TO BE TAKEN

03:23:41.290 --> 03:23:43.480
FOR SUBSTANTIATED VIOLATIONS.

03:23:43.480 --> 03:23:46.270
SAFE NURSE TO PATIENT RATIOS
ARE CRUCIAL

03:23:46.270 --> 03:23:47.470
FOR ENSURING THAT PATIENTS

03:23:47.470 --> 03:23:50.290
RECEIVE THE APPROPRIATE LEVEL OF
CARE AND ATTENTION.

03:23:50.290 --> 03:23:53.860
FAILURE TO ADHERE TO RATIOS
LEADS TO ERRORS,

03:23:53.860 --> 03:23:55.870
MAY LEAD TO DELAYS IN CARE

03:23:55.870 --> 03:23:58.120
AND COMPROMISED PATIENT SAFETY.

03:23:58.150 --> 03:24:01.180
IT'S OUR EXPECTATION THAT WITH
MORE TRANSPARENCY,

03:24:01.209 --> 03:24:02.950
HOSPITALS WILL ADHERE TO THE
STAFFING

03:24:02.950 --> 03:24:04.090
LAW IN ORDER TO MAINTAIN

03:24:04.090 --> 03:24:05.800
HIGH QUALITY CARE FOR PATIENTS

03:24:05.800 --> 03:24:07.720
AND AVOID NURSE BURNOUT.

03:24:07.750 --> 03:24:09.640
THIS BILL IS SUPPORTED BY NURSES

03:24:09.640 --> 03:24:11.470
AND LABOR UNIONS ACROSS
CALIFORNIA,

03:24:11.470 --> 03:24:14.980
AND HAS NO OPPOSITION WITH ME
TO TESTIFY IN

03:24:14.980 --> 03:24:17.980
SUPPORT OF THE MEASURE ARE
ALICIA AMBRIZ,

03:24:17.980 --> 03:24:19.720
IF I PRONOUNCE THAT CORRECTLY.

03:24:19.959 --> 03:24:20.950
CLOSE.

03:24:21.400 --> 03:24:23.140
I HATE TO MISPRONOUNCE NAMES.

03:24:23.140 --> 03:24:25.840
EUNUCH SECRETARY AT SAINT
FRANCIS MEDICAL CENTER,

03:24:25.840 --> 03:24:28.450
AND MATT LEGGETT, SEIU ADVOCATE.

03:24:30.910 --> 03:24:31.480
WITNESS.

03:24:31.480 --> 03:24:32.090
YOU HAVE TWO.

03:24:32.090 --> 03:24:32.470
MINUTES.

03:24:32.500 --> 03:24:33.100
OKAY.

03:24:33.100 --> 03:24:35.140
CAN YOU HEAR ME?

03:24:35.140 --> 03:24:35.530
IS IT ON?

03:24:35.530 --> 03:24:35.860
YES.

03:24:35.860 --> 03:24:36.280
IT'S ON.

03:24:36.280 --> 03:24:36.640
HI.

03:24:36.640 --> 03:24:37.330
GOOD AFTERNOON.

03:24:37.330 --> 03:24:37.780
THANK YOU.

03:24:37.780 --> 03:24:39.879
CHAIR ROTH AND MEMBERS OF THE
HEALTH COMMITTEE FOR

03:24:39.879 --> 03:24:43.810
THE OPPORTUNITY TO SPEAK IN
SUPPORT OF AB 2899.

03:24:44.230 --> 03:24:45.580
MY NAME IS ALICIA AMBRIZ.

03:24:45.580 --> 03:24:47.650
I AM A REGISTERED NURSE AND A
MEMBER

03:24:47.650 --> 03:24:49.540
OF THE UNITED NURSES
ASSOCIATIONS

03:24:49.540 --> 03:24:52.810
OF CALIFORNIA UNION OF HEALTH
CARE PROFESSIONALS.

03:24:52.870 --> 03:24:55.300
I'VE BEEN AN ACUTE OBSTETRICS

03:24:55.300 --> 03:24:57.459
NURSE CARE FOR 30 YEARS,

03:24:57.459 --> 03:24:59.530
AND I HAVE SEEN FIRSTHAND THE
CHALLENGES

03:24:59.530 --> 03:25:01.720
THAT THE UNDERSTAFFING CREATES,

03:25:01.720 --> 03:25:03.550
INCLUDING THE LONG TERM IMPACT

03:25:03.550 --> 03:25:05.620
IT HAS ON THE WORKING NURSE.

03:25:05.620 --> 03:25:07.570
WHEN A NURSE CONSISTENTLY WORKS

03:25:07.570 --> 03:25:08.920
IN AN UNDERSTAFFED UNIT,

03:25:08.920 --> 03:25:10.450
IF NOT ONLY PLACES TREMENDOUS

03:25:10.450 --> 03:25:12.010
STRAIN ON THE NURSE WHO

03:25:12.010 --> 03:25:14.709
IS NOW RESPONSIBLE FOR MANAGING
MORE PATIENTS,

03:25:14.709 --> 03:25:16.570
BUT IT ALSO DISRUPTS THE OVERALL

03:25:16.570 --> 03:25:18.580
FUNCTIONING OF THE UNIT.

03:25:18.580 --> 03:25:21.040
OVER TIME, THESE PERSISTENT
VIOLATIONS

03:25:21.040 --> 03:25:21.970
OF NURSE TO PATIENT

03:25:21.970 --> 03:25:25.240
RATIOS ERODE TRUST IN THE
REGULATORY SYSTEM.

03:25:25.240 --> 03:25:26.740
BECAUSE THE LAWS ESTABLISHED

03:25:26.740 --> 03:25:28.150
TO SAFEGUARD BOTH NURSES

03:25:28.150 --> 03:25:30.940
AND PATIENTS ARE NOT EFFECTIVELY
ENFORCED.

03:25:31.120 --> 03:25:33.850
AFTER COVID 19, THOUSANDS OF
NURSES

03:25:33.850 --> 03:25:35.200
LEFT THE PROFESSION BECAUSE

03:25:35.200 --> 03:25:38.379
OF UNSAFE STAFFING ASSIGNMENTS
THAT LED TO BURNOUT,

03:25:38.379 --> 03:25:41.440
A CHRONIC ISSUE ACROSS THE
UNITED STATES IN NURSING.

03:25:41.680 --> 03:25:44.290
AS A NURSE LEADER IN MY UNION
AND HOSPITAL,

03:25:44.290 --> 03:25:47.590
I HAVE SUBMITTED COMPLAINTS TO
CDPH NOTIFYING

03:25:47.590 --> 03:25:50.410
THE DEPARTMENT OF VIOLATIONS OF
THE STAFFING RATIO.

03:25:50.440 --> 03:25:52.840
UNFORTUNATELY, COMMUNICATION

03:25:52.840 --> 03:25:54.370
HAS PROVEN TO BE CHALLENGING

03:25:54.370 --> 03:25:55.870
AND THE OUTCOMES OF MY
COMPLAINTS,

03:25:55.870 --> 03:25:56.980
AS WELL AS THOSE FROM OTHER

03:25:56.980 --> 03:25:58.870
NURSES LACK TRANSPARENCY.

03:25:58.900 --> 03:26:00.730
THESE OUTCOMES HAVE BEEN
PERSISTENT

03:26:00.730 --> 03:26:02.890
FOR 20 YEARS AND MORE RECENTLY,

03:26:02.890 --> 03:26:04.240
WHEN FINES WERE INTRODUCED,

03:26:04.240 --> 03:26:07.629
HARDLY ANY HAVE BEEN ISSUED TO
THESE FACILITIES.

03:26:07.900 --> 03:26:12.010
AB 2899 BRINGS SUNLIGHT TO A
COMPLAINT INVESTIGATION

03:26:12.010 --> 03:26:13.300
PROCESS THAT CURRENTLY CREATES

03:26:13.300 --> 03:26:15.580
A LOT OF SUSPICION AND DISTRUST
AMONG

03:26:15.580 --> 03:26:17.800
THE NURSING STAFF AT HOSPITALS.

03:26:18.459 --> 03:26:20.410
CURRENTLY, WHEN THE CALIFORNIA
DEPARTMENT

03:26:20.410 --> 03:26:22.150
OF PUBLIC HEALTH DPH

03:26:22.180 --> 03:26:24.040
FINDS A SUBSTANTIATED VIOLATION

03:26:24.040 --> 03:26:25.510
OF NURSE STAFFING RATIOS,

03:26:25.510 --> 03:26:27.430
IT IS REQUIRED TO SEND
INFORMATION

03:26:27.430 --> 03:26:29.200
TO THE GENERAL ACUTE CARE
HOSPITAL

03:26:29.200 --> 03:26:31.150
REGARDING THE ACTION TO BE TAKEN

03:26:31.150 --> 03:26:32.560
BASED ON THAT VIOLATION,

03:26:32.560 --> 03:26:34.330
BUT THE PARTY FILING A REPORT OF

03:26:34.330 --> 03:26:35.980
A STAFFING VIOLATION, TYPICALLY,

03:26:35.980 --> 03:26:38.050
AN OVERWORKED NURSE IN THE
HOSPITAL,

03:26:38.050 --> 03:26:41.830
IS NOT ALERTED AS TO ANY ACTION
TAKEN BY A CDF.

03:26:42.490 --> 03:26:46.720
AB 2899 WILL CHANGE THAT BY
REQUIRING CDF TO PROVIDE

03:26:46.720 --> 03:26:48.250
THE SAME INFORMATION THAT WAS

03:26:48.250 --> 03:26:49.510
PROVIDED TO THE HOSPITAL,

03:26:49.510 --> 03:26:51.850
TO THE PERSON MAKING THE
COMPLAINT OR THEIR

03:26:51.850 --> 03:26:54.040
COLLECTIVE BARGAINING
REPRESENTATIVE.

03:26:54.340 --> 03:26:55.030
THIS WAY.

03:26:55.030 --> 03:26:55.840
WRAP IT UP.

03:26:55.840 --> 03:26:56.440
OH, SORRY.

03:26:56.440 --> 03:26:58.750
OKAY, SO IT IS IMPORTANT TO NOTE
THAT AB

03:26:58.750 --> 03:27:00.760
DOES NOT ESTABLISH ANY NEW
VIOLATION,

03:27:00.760 --> 03:27:02.920
PENALTIES OR ENFORCEMENT
REQUIREMENTS.

03:27:02.920 --> 03:27:04.870
IT JUST MERELY REQUIRES THE
DISSEMINATION

03:27:04.870 --> 03:27:05.950
OF INFORMATION

03:27:05.950 --> 03:27:08.379
ABOUT THE CURRENT PROCESS
REGARDING VIOLATIONS.

03:27:08.379 --> 03:27:10.600
MOREOVER, IT IS LIMITED IN SCOPE

03:27:11.110 --> 03:27:12.490
TO IMPOSE ANY REQUIREMENTS

03:27:12.490 --> 03:27:15.430
